on: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LYyBDscCwdTXxWnYZaCqPY","tree":{"sha":"06e9c7ef534d67692bb50796b985ea38a8fb33ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/git/trees/06e9c7ef534d67692bb50796b985ea38a8fb33ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/git/commits/d1023061339b6effeab87cbf7b9fbd12f5dcb619","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commit/d1023061339b6effeab87cbf7b9fbd12f5dcb619","node_id":"C_kwDOP4ae9doAKGQxMDIzMDYxMzM5YjZlZmZlYWI4N2NiZjdiOWZiZDEyZjVkY2I2MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commit/837acb2e71e92523101d59db170684a33e165689","sha":"837acb2e71e92523101d59db170684a33e165689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commits/837acb2e71e92523101d59db170684a33e165689"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commit/06b52e9b5acab3500adbd12e266eb3ac0c3cbb7c","sha":"06b52e9b5acab3500adbd12e266eb3ac0c3cbb7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commits/06b52e9b5acab3500adbd12e266eb3ac0c3cbb7c"}],"sha":"d1023061339b6effeab87cbf7b9fbd12f5dcb619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commits/d1023061339b6effeab87cbf7b9fbd12f5dcb619"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69564524?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JarrodJackson98","id":69564524,"login":"JarrodJackson98","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NTY0NTI0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JarrodJackson98","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/commits/0e1d99b8a0fb4cae504f65cc0370c9b239b17b3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:09:27Z","email":"69564524+JarrodJackson98@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JarrodJackson98"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:09:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep the Tank tile when its sensor has no reading, and show a sensor fault (#4)\n\nA tank level sensor below its 4 mA zero (3.73 mA on the live skid) publishes\nno level, and the Tank tile disappeared with it, so the operator could not\ntell \"no sensor\" from \"no tank\" and lost the gear needed to fix it. Like the\nSkid tile, the Tank tile now stays whenever tank_level_app is set, in every\nmode: a missing level reads \"--\" with an empty Fill bar, never the last value.\n\nWhen the tank app publishes sensor_fault (\"under_range\"), the tile also shows\na red SENSOR FAULT badge in its heading, a red edge, and the reason under the\nreadings (\"Signal below range (3.73 mA)\", from raw_level_reading). No level is\nshown while it is set. The alarm gear and the Sensor tab stay reachable, and\nthe Sensor tab shows the live loop current. An older tank app without the tag\ngets the \"--\" tile and no badge.\n\nThe mock host gains tankfault=1 (fault) and tankfault=old (older tank app,\nno reading). The layout checks cover both at every size, in Touch and Read\nOnly, with the alarm gear and Sensor tab, with and without the insets.\nTANK_SHOTS=dir saves the 1024x600 screenshots.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0138AFJWs8mLc6YF5SDseHvu\n\nCo-authored-by: Jarrod <jarrod@span-eng.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9873078743b34872dec224f73e81afb2a34bd13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/git/trees/f9873078743b34872dec224f73e81afb2a34bd13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getdoover/sia-local-control-ui/git/commits/0e1d99b8a0fb4cae504f65cc0370c9b239b17b3f","verification":{"payload":"tree f9873078743b34872dec224f73e81afb2a34bd13\nparent 837acb2e71e92523101d59db170684a33e165689\nauthor JarrodJackson98 <69564524+JarrodJackson98@users.noreply.github.com> 1790845767 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790845767 +1000\n\nKeep the Tank tile when its sensor has no reading, and show a sensor fault (#4)\n\nA tank level sensor below its 4 mA zero (3.73 mA on the live skid) publishes\nno level, and the Tank tile disappeared with it, so the operator could not\ntell \"no sensor\" from \"no tank\" and lost the gear needed to fix it. Like the\nSkid tile, the Tank tile now stays whenever tank_level_app is set, in every\nmode: a missing level reads \"--\" with an empty Fill bar, never the last value.\n\nWhen the tank app publishes sensor_fault (\"under_range\"), the tile also shows\na red SENSOR FAULT badge in its heading, a red edge, and the reason under the\nreadings (\"Signal below range (3.73 mA)\", from raw_level_reading). No level is\nshown while it is set. The alarm gear and the Sensor tab stay reachable, and\nthe Sensor tab shows the live loop current. An older tank app without the tag\ngets the \"--\" tile and no badge.\n\nThe mock host gains tankfault=1 (fault) and tankfault=old (older tank app,\nno reading). The layout checks cover both at every size, in Touch and Read\nOnly, with the alarm gear and Sensor tab, with and without the insets.\nTANK_SHOTS=dir saves the 1024x600 screenshots.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0138AFJWs8mLc6YF5SDseHvu\n\nCo-authored-by: Jarro