b12052a609acbb162219e250e8dbc7ebe5ebb965","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/git/trees/b12052a609acbb162219e250e8dbc7ebe5ebb965"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/git/commits/a8a33ce51e94f4984e753e341776bcd21017fb90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commit/a8a33ce51e94f4984e753e341776bcd21017fb90","node_id":"C_kwDOP4y8dtoAKGE4YTMzY2U1MWU5NGY0OTg0ZTc1M2UzNDE3NzZiY2QyMTAxN2ZiOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commit/851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be","sha":"851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commits/851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be"}],"sha":"a8a33ce51e94f4984e753e341776bcd21017fb90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commits/a8a33ce51e94f4984e753e341776bcd21017fb90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commits/851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-26T01:54:33Z","email":"hugo.burton@westpac.com.au","name":"Hugo Burton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-26T01:54:33Z","email":"hugo.burton@westpac.com.au","name":"Hugo Burton"},"message":"fix: resolve shared module context duplication in dev mode (react-router, SSO, etc.)\n\nThree bugs were causing shared modules to create duplicate instances in dev\nmode, breaking React contexts (LocationContext, ReactReduxContext, SSO\nselectors, etc.) when MFEs are loaded by a host SPA.\n\n## Bug 1: async config hook not awaited (index.ts)\n\nThe main plugin''s config hook called sub-plugin config hooks without\n`await`. The devExposePlugin''s config hook is async (it calls\n`getModuleExportNames()`), so sharedModuleMeta was never populated\nbefore configureServer ran. This meant the .vite/deps/ response\nmiddleware was never registered, and pre-bundled shared modules were\nserved completely unpatched.\n\nFix: make the config hook async and await each sub-plugin''s config.\n\n## Bug 2: version resolution skipped for remotes (remote-development.ts)\n\nThe version resolution guard `(isHost || isShared) && !isRemote`\nprevented version resolution when the app is a remote, even if it also\nhas shared modules. Since MFEs are always remotes (they have `exposes`)\nAND have shared modules, shared module versions were never resolved,\nresulting in `''undefined''` version strings in the shareScope.\n\nFix: remove the `!isRemote` guard — resolve versions whenever shared\nmodules are configured.\n\n## Bug 3: ESM shared modules staying pre-bundled (expose-development.ts)\n\nWhen a shared ESM module stays pre-bundled in .vite/deps/, other\npre-bundled deps import its internal chunks directly, bypassing the\nshared facade. This creates duplicate module instances — e.g. two\nLocationContext objects for react-router, two SSO selector stores.\n\nThe fix excludes ALL non-CJS shared modules from dep optimization so\nthe resolveId/load virtual wrapper intercepts every import (including\nfrom other pre-bundled deps). Non-shared bare-specifier dependencies\nfound in the entry or internal chunks are force-included via\noptimizeDeps.include so the browser can load them.\n\nOne exception: modules whose entry uses `export * from \"cjs-pkg\"`\n(e.g. @reduxjs/toolkit does `export * from \"redux\"`) cannot be\nexcluded. `export *` requires the target module to expose static named\nESM exports, but CJS modules pre-bundled by Vite only have a default\nexport. These modules stay pre-bundled and are patched by the\n.vite/deps/ response middleware.\n\n### Module strategy summary:\n\n| Module                | Strategy      | Reason                          |\n|-----------------------|---------------|---------------------------------|\n| react, react-dom,     | Pre-bundled   | CJS — `t` factory patched by    |\n| react-redux, zustand  |               | middleware                      |\n| @reduxjs/toolkit      | Pre-bundled   | `export * from \"redux\"` (CJS)   |\n| react-router          | Excluded      | Pure relative imports in entry  |\n| @mesh-tenant-westpac- | Excluded      | ESM, no `export *` from CJS     |\n| viteframework/sso     |               |                                 |\n\nAmp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-019d2514-dba5-7798-87df-bc8ab0c8928e\nCo-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>","tree":{"sha":"a257c566f2b4d494b605a47698e1d49b43f6d3d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/git/trees/a257c566f2b4d494b605a47698e1d49b43f6d3d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/git/commits/851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commit/851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be","node_id":"C_kwDOP4y8dtoAKDg1MTQ5NGZmMTlmZmI1MjllYzcyMWZmOTk2MTM5ZjFmOWRmZjU4YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commit/368b26c47b1c928e1dd47b5b45d5e94284bd957a","sha":"368b26c47b1c928e1dd47b5b45d5e94284bd957a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commits/368b26c47b1c928e1dd47b5b45d5e94284bd957a"}],"sha":"851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hugs7/vite-plugin-federation/commits/851494ff19ffb529ec721ff996139f1f9dff58be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com