143301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","id":198982749,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/commit/2e93d687b11e966e5f56870c188534caeb26882f","node_id":"C_kwDOP5Duu9oAKDJlOTNkNjg3YjExZTk2NmU1ZjU2ODcwYzE4ODUzNGNhZWIyNjg4MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/commit/19a15cb427d457f7e88bddb7624a2d24b2f70161","sha":"19a15cb427d457f7e88bddb7624a2d24b2f70161","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/commits/19a15cb427d457f7e88bddb7624a2d24b2f70161"}],"sha":"2e93d687b11e966e5f56870c188534caeb26882f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/commits/2e93d687b11e966e5f56870c188534caeb26882f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","id":198982749,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/commits/19a15cb427d457f7e88bddb7624a2d24b2f70161/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-01T12:04:00Z","email":"198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-01T12:04:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Implement secure backend middleware for CommerceTools with comprehensive testing, documentation, Terraform integration, and fully automated CI/CD workflows (#9)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: implement secure backend middleware for CommerceTools\n\n- Add comprehensive type definitions for reviews, auth, and CommerceTools\n- Implement authentication middleware with JWT support\n- Add rate limiting middleware (10 req/min general, 5 req/min write ops)\n- Create validation middleware with input sanitization\n- Implement CommerceTools service with mock data for POC\n- Add review and auth controllers with full CRUD operations\n- Configure Swagger/OpenAPI documentation\n- Implement structured logging with Winston\n- Add comprehensive tests with 87.89% coverage (51 tests passing)\n- Configure Jest with ts-jest for TypeScript testing\n- Add security features: Helmet, CORS, rate-limiting, XSS protection\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: add comprehensive API documentation and security guidelines\n\n- Add detailed backend README with examples and architecture\n- Create API examples document with JavaScript, TypeScript, and React code samples\n- Add Security & GDPR compliance checklist with pre-production requirements\n- Create JSON schemas for review input/output validation\n- Add .env.example with all configuration options\n- Document authentication flow, error handling, and rate limiting\n- Include GDPR data minimization and protection guidelines\n- Add security incident response procedures\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: add implementation summary and final verification\n\n- Add comprehensive implementation summary document\n- Verify server starts successfully\n- Test all main endpoints working correctly\n- Document all 36 files created/modified\n- List key achievements and technical metrics\n- Provide production readiness checklist\n- Include next steps and learning resources\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: add comprehensive CI/CD and deployment documentation\n\n- Create detailed DEPLOYMENT.md with step-by-step instructions\n- Document GCP prerequisites and setup\n- Add GitHub Actions configuration guide\n- Include complete environment variables reference\n- Add CI/CD workflow explanation and customization guide\n- Document manual deployment options\n- Include troubleshooting section and common issues\n- Update README.md with Deployment and CI/CD sections\n- Link to deployment guide from root README\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: integrate backend deployment with Terraform and document GitHub Actions variables\n\n- Create backend.tf with complete backend infrastructure configuration\n- Add backend-specific variables to variables.tf (secrets, resources, config)\n- Update outputs.tf with backend-specific outputs (health check, API docs URLs)\n- Create terraform.tfvars examples for preview and production environments\n- Create comprehensive GITHUB_ACTIONS_VARIABLES.md guide\n- Update DEPLOYMENT.md with Terraform integration section\n- Update infra/README.md with detailed backend configuration documentation\n- Document all required GitHub secrets and repository variables\n- Provide complete variable mapping between GitHub Actions and Terraform\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: integrate GitHub Actions workflows with Terraform infrastructure\n\n- Update pr-preview.yml to use Terraform for infrastructure provisioning\n- Update pr-cleanup.yml to use Terraform destroy for cleanup\n- Add Terraform setup step (v1.6.0) to both workflows\n- Pass all required variables to Terraform (project_id, region, service_name, environment)\n- Use environment variables for sensitive Terraform variables (TF_VAR_*)\n- Get service URLs from Terraform outputs instead of gcloud\n- Remove manual gcloud deploy commands in favor of Terraform\n- Add comprehensive Terraform Integration section to GITHUB_ACTIONS_VARIABLES.md\n- Document complete variable flow (GitHub → Terraform)\n- Add workflow overview and configuration examples\n- Update DEPLOYMENT.md CI/CD section with Terraform integration details\n- Document preview vs production deployment differences\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: resolve Terraform resource conflict between main.tf and backend.tf\n\n- Remove duplicate backend service from main.tf (conflicts with backend.tf)\n- backend.tf defines google_cloud_run_service.backend_api with full config\n- main.tf was creating google_cloud_run_service.backend with same name\n- Keep only backend_api resource which has comprehensive configuration\n- Remove backend_noauth IAM from main.tf (already in backend.tf)\n- Update infra/README.md import command to use backend_api resource\n- This fixes terraform plan failures due to duplicate resource definitions\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: resolve Terraform deprecation warnings and sensitive value errors\n\n- Replace deprecated ''automatic = true'' with ''auto {}'' in all secret replication blocks (backend.tf)\n- Remove unused ''secrets'' variable resources from main.tf (api_keys secret and version)\n- Secrets are now fully managed in backend.tf with proper configuration\n- Fix \"sensitive value in for_each\" error by removing var.secrets iteration\n- All 4 deprecation warnings resolved (jwt_secret, ctp_project_key, ctp_client_id, ctp_client_secret)\n- Terraform plan should now succeed without warnings or errors\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: remove explicit port declaration from backend Cloud Run service\n\n- Remove ports block from backend_api service in backend.tf\n- Cloud Run automatically detects port from PORT environment variable (8080)\n- Explicit port declaration is redundant and can cause issues\n- Follow Cloud Run best practices for port configuration\n\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove ports\n\n* fix: remove PORT environment variable from frontend Cloud Run service\n\n* Update test urls\n\n* Adding back timeouts\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Gallad51 <67849897+Gallad51@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"09e7fe8f827362c12e026f28b95f3c7e66ece867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/git/trees/09e7fe8f827362c12e026f28b95f3c7e66ece867"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Gallad51/POC-Rating-and-review-CommerceTools/git/commits/19a15cb427d457f7e88bddb7624a2d24b2f70161","verification":{"payload":"tree 09e7fe8f827362c12e026f28b95f3c7e66ece867\nparent 05aec816964fe2f71dce3bb6edbccb0c4cee13b6\nauthor Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com> 1759320240 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1759320240 +0200\n\nfeat: Implement secure backend