ithub-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"1b8e2bc177d93bfeb44099a1cf2db22e0f5c1c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/1b8e2bc177d93bfeb44099a1cf2db22e0f5c1c3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/1437b44d04e14563e35ecaf0cbfb5898957a4e89","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b8e2bc177d93bfeb44099a1cf2db22e0f5c1c3d\nparent d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5\nauthor github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650429 -0700\ncommitter github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789650429 -0700\n\nchore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLDaOUaEAvRANFoNpCRgpPHAN541RrcGvfIOHobIYNWUar/c10eB9udVBWjpoB8I6q\n2xYrO6olJdLVx4fAZ8pAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/1437b44d04e14563e35ecaf0cbfb5898957a4e89","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDE0MzdiNDRkMDRlMTQ1NjNlMzVlY2FmMGNiZmI1ODk4OTU3YTRlODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5","sha":"d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5"}],"sha":"1437b44d04e14563e35ecaf0cbfb5898957a4e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/1437b44d04e14563e35ecaf0cbfb5898957a4e89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/f1f7e6a2c3643a138ca62a7c77ca544ecaf551ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T00:20:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T00:20:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(plan-notes): match the pass footer the way the contract now says\n\nTenHands wrote the footer shape down (their autoland-v3.md §11) after the\nlast round, so this stops being a guess at their format and becomes the\nsame bargain struck on both sides: permissive on the values, tight on the\nshape.\n\nThe tail was `[separator].*`, which also swallowed\n\n    — pass 2 · confidence 0.8 and then some\n\na line THEY keep as the human''s words — their pattern is `$`-anchored per\nline, so the whole line must match. That divergence ran in the direction\nthat loses a human''s answer rather than merely mis-badging it, which is\nthe worse of the two silent failures. The tail is now `separator label\nvalue` and then end-of-line, which lands on their answers for every case\nat the boundary.\n\n`,` is no longer a separator either: human prose is full of commas, and\n`— pass 2, some note` was being eaten.\n\nChecking that against the old pattern turned up a third case it got\nwrong: a footer with TRAILING WHITESPACE did not strip at all, because\nthe wildcard tail never matched and `$` then failed on the spaces. An\neditor adding or trimming a space decided whether the runner wake fired.\nNow `\\s*$`.\n\nAlso pins the multi-footer document. A human can paste an older footer\nback above the current one, and that shape ran TenHands'' own pass counter\nBACKWARDS — their reader took the first footer, their writer the last.\nNothing here reads the number, so there is no authoritative-footer\nquestion to get wrong; every match is removed rather than the first or\nthe last, and the test says so.","tree":{"sha":"a1b4a252c0b5f89b026d507cd9e258b9ad3c8a9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/a1b4a252c0b5f89b026d507cd9e258b9ad3c8a9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/f1f7e6a2c3643a138ca62a7c77ca544ecaf551ad","verification":{"payload":"tree a1b4a252c0b5f89b026d507cd9e258b9ad3c8a9c\nparent 13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789604401 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789604401 -0700\n\nfix(plan-notes): match the pass footer the way the contract now says\n\nTenHands wrote the footer shape down (their autoland-v3.md §11) after the\nlast round, so this stops being a guess at their format and becomes the\nsame bargain struck on both sides: permissive on the values, tight on the\nshape.\n\nThe tail was `[separator].*`, which also swallowed\n\n    — pass 2 · confidence 0.8 and then some\n\na line THEY keep as the human''s words — their pattern is `$`-anchored per\nline, so the whole line must match. That divergence ran in the direction\nthat loses a human''s answer rather than merely mis-badging it, which is\nthe worse of the two silent failures. The tail is now `separator label\nvalue` and then end-of-line, which lands on their answers for every case\nat the boundary.\n\n`,` is no longer a separator either: human prose is full of commas, and\n`— pass 2, some note` was being eaten.\n\nChecking that against the old pattern turned up a third case it got\nwrong: a footer with TRAILING WHITESPACE did not strip at all, because\nthe wildcard tail never matched and `$` then failed on the spaces. An\neditor adding or trimming a space decided whether the runner wake fired.\nNow `\\s*$`.\n\nAlso pins the multi-footer document. A human can paste an older footer\nback above the current one, and that shape ran TenHands'' own pass counter\nBACKWARDS — their reader took the first footer, their writer the last.\nNothing here reads the number, so there is no authoritative-footer\nquestion to get wrong; every match is removed rather than the first or\nthe last, and the test says so.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJ9wJffnA1Bfsao6Q0ss7j6NcDqVrDsDXs9jKJbNL7YPaI08VD+yqeCQ2Lh97ca0C/\ndZ5nA0k30k5AH82L4NdAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T00:20:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/f1f7e6a2c3643a138ca62a7c77ca544ecaf551ad","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGYxZjdlNmEyYzM2NDNhMTM4Y2E2MmE3Yzc3Y2E1NDRlY2FmNTUxYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5","sha":"13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5"}],"sha":"f1f7e6a2c3643a138ca62a7c77ca544ecaf551ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/f1f7e6a2c3643a138ca62a7c77ca544ecaf551ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:34:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T20:34:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(plan-notes): treat TenHands'' pass footer as bookkeeping, not a reply\n\nEvery plan document TenHands renders ends with a bookkeeping line:\n\n    — pass 1\n    — pass 2 · confidence 0.8\n\n`## Questions` is the last section of any plan proposing no acceptance\ncriteria, so the footer lands inside its body — where parseQuestionsBody\nsees an item, a blank line and prose, which is byte-for-byte the shape of\na human''s trailing reply. It filed our correspondent''s own footer as the\nhuman''s answer.\n\nThe badge was the visible half. The damage was the wake: it made\nquestionsAnswered true the moment the plan was written, so when the human\nactually answered there was no false -> true transition for\nnotesWriteClosesQuestions, no repository_dispatch, and the ~15 minute cron\ntail came back for exactly the case §5.1 exists to remove. The predicate\nwas working as designed and being fed a document whose state was already\nwrong.\n\nStrip the footer in parsePlanNotes, before any sectioning. Stripped\nwherever it stands rather than only when trailing: appendAnswerToNotes puts\na reply AFTER the footer when Questions is the last section, so a\ntrailing-only rule stops matching the moment someone answers and folds our\nbookkeeping into their reply text. Fence-aware like every other line rule\nhere, so a plan documenting the format keeps it. Nothing rewrites the\nstored notes — the toggle and the editor both work from the raw string — so\nthe pass counter survives a round trip through the UI.\n\nPermissive on the values, tight on the structure: a strict pattern that\nfailed to match on a junk confidence would silently restore the whole bug,\nwhich is the lesson TenHands learned when it reset their pass counter.\n\nThe approval path was never affected — an unticked box short-circuits\nbefore the reply check — but it is the primary path, so it is pinned too.\nAlso fixes a count that was under-reporting: a footed section with both a\nprose question and an unticked box read as 1 open ask, not 2.\n\nWhile here, make the plan-review fixtures authoritative. boardId derives\nfrom testId, which is stable across runs, and the dev stack''s D1 outlives\nthe suite, so a re-run found rows a previous run had answered and the POST\nleft them as they were — a half-answered fixture that fails looking exactly\nlike a parser bug.","tree":{"sha":"79773446e706dd48fce8527ac3b61dd4e2150069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/79773446e706dd48fce8527ac3b61dd4e2150069"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 79773446e706dd48fce8527ac3b61dd4e2150069\nparent 6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789590862 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789590862 -0700\n\nfix(plan-notes): treat TenHands'' pass footer as bookkeeping, not a reply\n\nEvery plan document TenHands renders ends with a bookkeeping line:\n\n    — pass 1\n    — pass 2 · confidence 0.8\n\n`## Questions` is the last section of any plan proposing no acceptance\ncriteria, so the footer lands inside its body — where parseQuestionsBody\nsees an item, a blank line and prose, which is byte-for-byte the shape of\na human''s trailing reply. It filed our correspondent''s own footer as the\nhuman''s answer.\n\nThe badge was the visible half. The damage was the wake: it made\nquestionsAnswered true the moment the plan was written, so when the human\nactually answered there was no false -> true transition for\nnotesWriteClosesQuestions, no repository_dispatch, and the ~15 minute cron\ntail came back for exactly the case §5.1 exists to remove. The predicate\nwas working as designed and being fed a document whose state was already\nwrong.\n\nStrip the footer in parsePlanNotes, before any sectioning. Stripped\nwherever it stands rather than only when trailing: appendAnswerToNotes puts\na reply AFTER the footer when Questions is the last section, so a\ntrailing-only rule stops matching the moment someone answers and folds our\nbookkeeping into their reply text. Fence-aware like every other line rule\nhere, so a plan documenting the format keeps it. Nothing rewrites the\nstored notes — the toggle and the editor both work from the raw string — so\nthe pass counter survives a round trip through the UI.\n\nPermissive on the values, tight on the structure: a strict pattern that\nfailed to match on a junk confidence would silently restore the whole bug,\nwhich is the lesson TenHands learned when it reset their pass counter.\n\nThe approval path was never affected — an unticked box short-circuits\nbefore the reply check — but it is the primary path, so it is pinned too.\nAlso fixes a count that was under-reporting: a footed section with both a\nprose question and an unticked box read as 1 open ask, not 2.\n\nWhile here, make the plan-review fixtures authoritative. boardId derives\nfrom testId, which is stable across runs, and the dev stack''s D1 outlives\nthe suite, so a re-run found rows a previous run had answered and the POST\nleft them as they were — a half-answered fixture that fails looking exactly\nlike a parser bug.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHEI8zPW8c1vX6oljeguG8nzwlpYAhsSjgFTPpbb0iguRkpVTpluLn65cJVV8CS1t2\nfqZqvPWTsp+/t3K6nzDwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T20:35:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDEzYjg2MmE0YjE0NzllMDFjNmFlNTgyYjBjMjUwMjJmZTE5ZjI5YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9","sha":"6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9"}],"sha":"13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/13b862a4b1479e01c6ae582b0c25022fe19f29b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T05:14:13Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T05:14:13Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"docs(automation): migration 0007 is a hard deploy-order dependency\n\nMeasured rather than assumed: the real worker booted against migrations\n0002-0006 answers `500 ERR_SQLITE_ERROR` on GET /boards, because `status` is\nin the SELECT list of every task read. So this is not \"the chip won''t render\nuntil the migration lands\" — the app does not load at all.\n\nNothing in CI runs migrations here and the worker does not self-migrate\n(ensureInitialized only scaffolds a user''s rows), so the ordering is on\nwhoever deploys. Said so in the migration itself and in the reply doc, where\nthe previous wording understated it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"909164b0460c4a8c0788de264b964eba82f4268b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/909164b0460c4a8c0788de264b964eba82f4268b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9","verification":{"payload":"tree 909164b0460c4a8c0788de264b964eba82f4268b\nparent 080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789535653 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789535653 -0700\n\ndocs(automation): migration 0007 is a hard deploy-order dependency\n\nMeasured rather than assumed: the real worker booted against migrations\n0002-0006 answers `500 ERR_SQLITE_ERROR` on GET /boards, because `status` is\nin the SELECT list of every task read. So this is not \"the chip won''t render\nuntil the migration lands\" — the app does not load at all.\n\nNothing in CI runs migrations here and the worker does not self-migrate\n(ensureInitialized only scaffolds a user''s rows), so the ordering is on\nwhoever deploys. Said so in the migration itself and in the reply doc, where\nthe previous wording understated it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQM4F0CVrsCwcalmSUUQNRtZ92Pt7IsAYtygYcN3MizpGCY7J6WOqMuL6nzSSHaOy+J\nELivJBdgjNbeQ6iAK2ag4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T20:35:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDZmYjA4YTdkOTkwNjk0OWVkMWU0OWNjMWNlOGQ3OGVjOTMyMWQ1YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f","sha":"080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f"}],"sha":"6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6fb08a7d9906949ed1e49cc1ce8d78ec9321d5a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T05:12:37Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T05:13:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(automation): autoland v3 — notes guard, wake, status chip, approval\n\nTenHands is turning the autoland board axis ninety degrees: one board, lanes\nbecome REPOS, and pipeline state leaves the tag system entirely (a task carries\nexactly one tag and it must be a lane, so there is no second axis to move it\nto). Five things have to exist on our side for that to work.\n\n1. `ifNotesHash` on release — the blocking one. `ifCurrentLane` guards a\n   release against a human retagging mid-claim; with every lane editableBy\n   user there are no agent lanes left to give `notes` mutual exclusion, so the\n   same hazard moves to the plan document. A release that rewrote it would\n   destroy a reply typed while the agent worked, and that text is versioned\n   nowhere. Hash-compare-then-write in the runner is a race, not a guard —\n   only the server can compare and write atomically. Mismatch → 409\n   NOTES_CHANGED, nothing written, claim kept, `currentNotesHash` returned.\n   Digest is hex SHA-256 of the UTF-8 notes, absent notes hashing as \"\".\n\n2. The runner wake on a notes write. `laneOpts` was built from `''tag'' in\n   input`, so a notes-only update reached no hook — invisible while every\n   human handoff was a drag, fatal when answering IS the handoff. Fires on the\n   TRANSITION of `questionsAnswered` (false→true), never the state: the popout\n   autosaves, so firing on the state is a dispatch per keystroke. Payload\n   gains `reason` (additive, ignorable).\n\n3. `status` as a first-class field + a chip. Its own column, not\n   `metadata.<pipeline>.status` — a card renderer must not need one pipeline''s\n   metadata key to draw a chip. Closed `kind` set, validated (422\n   STATUS_INVALID), three-way like notes/metadata. Accepted on set-lane too so\n   a long job reports progress without dropping its lease.\n\n4. Task-list items render as checkboxes, plus an Approve button. Tapping\n   writes the same bytes a human typing `- [x]` would — one character inside\n   the brackets, every other byte copied through. No approvals table, no\n   metadata.approved. `questionsAnswered`/`openQuestionCount` learn checkbox\n   items (an unticked box is an open ask, a ticked one is its own answer, and\n   a section with none behaves exactly as before) — required, or approving\n   would never fire the wake in (2).\n\n5. `claimed` on the board read the UI actually calls, and on the card. It has\n   been in the hydrated agent read since v1 and nothing has ever rendered it.\n\nPushed back on fetching the status `kind` vocabulary from the presets\nendpoint: a lane label is data because it renders as text, but a `kind` is a\nstyling contract that resolves to code, and fetching it would also make a\ntypo''d kind unvalidatable. Reasoning and the §10 answer (lanes optional on a\nPRESET, still required by validateLaneSet — an example lane set would make\ndetectPresetUpdate report every task as stranded) are in\ndocs/planning/autoland-v3-reply.md.\n\nVerified against real D1 and a real browser, no mocks in the assertions: 30\nchecks in autoland-v3-verify (including the human''s text read straight out of\nD1 after a refused release), 84 in lane-dispatch-verify with fetch stubbed, 34\non the predicates, and 5 Playwright specs. Full suite green — every worker\nharness and 158 e2e.\n\nNOTE: worker/migrations/0007_task_status.sql must be applied to production D1\nby hand; nothing in CI runs migrations here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b31a3d53c7a2126874d59646505899933695a1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/5b31a3d53c7a2126874d59646505899933695a1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b31a3d53c7a2126874d59646505899933695a1e\nparent aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789535557 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789535590 -0700\n\nfeat(automation): autoland v3 — notes guard, wake, status chip, approval\n\nTenHands is turning the autoland board axis ninety degrees: one board, lanes\nbecome REPOS, and pipeline state leaves the tag system entirely (a task carries\nexactly one tag and it must be a lane, so there is no second axis to move it\nto). Five things have to exist on our side for that to work.\n\n1. `ifNotesHash` on release — the blocking one. `ifCurrentLane` guards a\n   release against a human retagging mid-claim; with every lane editableBy\n   user there are no agent lanes left to give `notes` mutual exclusion, so the\n   same hazard moves to the plan document. A release that rewrote it would\n   destroy a reply typed while the agent worked, and that text is versioned\n   nowhere. Hash-compare-then-write in the runner is a race, not a guard —\n   only the server can compare and write atomically. Mismatch → 409\n   NOTES_CHANGED, nothing written, claim kept, `currentNotesHash` returned.\n   Digest is hex SHA-256 of the UTF-8 notes, absent notes hashing as \"\".\n\n2. The runner wake on a notes write. `laneOpts` was built from `''tag'' in\n   input`, so a notes-only update reached no hook — invisible while every\n   human handoff was a drag, fatal when answering IS the handoff. Fires on the\n   TRANSITION of `questionsAnswered` (false→true), never the state: the popout\n   autosaves, so firing on the state is a dispatch per keystroke. Payload\n   gains `reason` (additive, ignorable).\n\n3. `status` as a first-class field + a chip. Its own column, not\n   `metadata.<pipeline>.status` — a card renderer must not need one pipeline''s\n   metadata key to draw a chip. Closed `kind` set, validated (422\n   STATUS_INVALID), three-way like notes/metadata. Accepted on set-lane too so\n   a long job reports progress without dropping its lease.\n\n4. Task-list items render as checkboxes, plus an Approve button. Tapping\n   writes the same bytes a human typing `- [x]` would — one character inside\n   the brackets, every other byte copied through. No approvals table, no\n   metadata.approved. `questionsAnswered`/`openQuestionCount` learn checkbox\n   items (an unticked box is an open ask, a ticked one is its own answer, and\n   a section with none behaves exactly as before) — required, or approving\n   would never fire the wake in (2).\n\n5. `claimed` on the board read the UI actually calls, and on the card. It has\n   been in the hydrated agent read since v1 and nothing has ever rendered it.\n\nPushed back on fetching the status `kind` vocabulary from the presets\nendpoint: a lane label is data because it renders as text, but a `kind` is a\nstyling contract that resolves to code, and fetching it would also make a\ntypo''d kind unvalidatable. Reasoning and the §10 answer (lanes optional on a\nPRESET, still required by validateLaneSet — an example lane set would make\ndetectPresetUpdate report every task as stranded) are in\ndocs/planning/autoland-v3-reply.md.\n\nVerified against real D1 and a real browser, no mocks in the assertions: 30\nchecks in autoland-v3-verify (including the human''s text read straight out of\nD1 after a refused release), 84 in lane-dispatch-verify with fetch stubbed, 34\non the predicates, and 5 Playwright specs. Full suite green — every worker\nharness and 158 e2e.\n\nNOTE: worker/migrations/0007_task_status.sql must be applied to production D1\nby hand; nothing in CI runs migrations here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNV5FOEGRVjBGgtj/YA3Ln1SDhDzVl6N5X4R5x4aEgDpUSthDow7cTw2kK5YY3ewe+\nPGAK7CXYc43yk9TpcQOQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T20:35:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDA4MDE3MmJjMTY2NDg0Y2FmNjZhNTQ2MDZjNzJiMjYxMDZjMzljM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","sha":"aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8"}],"sha":"080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/080172bc166484caf66a54606c72b26106c39c3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T04:52:50Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T04:53:24Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(boards): select several boards and delete them in one confirmation\n\nPer-board confirmations are what sent a user to Chrome''s \"prevent this page\nfrom creating additional dialogs\" checkbox in the first place, which then made\nevery delete a silent no-op. The previous two commits made the dialog ours so\nit cannot be switched off; this removes the reason to want it switched off.\n\nRows in Edit Boards get a checkbox, with a select-all and a bulk bar per group.\nThe bar''s verb comes from the row''s own action — owned boards delete, boards\nshared with you leave — so a selection can never mean two different things at\nonce, and `main`, which has no destructive action, has no checkbox.\n\nOne confirmation for the batch, naming every board it will destroy: a bulk\nconfirm that only says \"3 boards\" asks the user to trust a count they cannot\ncheck, and the batch is irreversible. Six names, then a count.\n\nThe single-row button routes through the same path with a one-board list, so\nthere is one confirm, one executor and one reporter rather than a batch path\nthat drifts from the single path.\n\nDetails that are load-bearing:\n\n- Selection is keyed by board ID. The list re-sorts on pin and re-filters on\n  search; a selection addressed by position would follow whichever row moved\n  into the slot.\n- A selection survives filtering, and the bar says how many selected rows the\n  search is hiding — a count that disagrees with the screen reads as a bug.\n- The bar stays rendered whenever anything is selected, even when the filter\n  leaves fewer than two rows, or the only control that can act on or clear the\n  selection would vanish and strand it.\n- The batch runs SEQUENTIALLY and keeps going past a failure. Each delete ends\n  in a reload and those share a sequence guard that discards superseded\n  results, so concurrent deletes would let timing pick the winner. Boards that\n  fail stay checked and are named in an error toast; the rest are cleared.\n\nUnification, same commit: ClearTagModal is deleted and folded into\nConfirmModal. It was a bespoke component for a destructive confirm, which is\nwhat ConfirmModal now is for every other one.\n\nCLAUDE.md gets the rule: no alert/confirm/prompt (eslint enforces it), what to\nuse instead for each kind of message, and the detail that catches people out —\nevery write is optimistic, so a server refusal goes to onSyncError and the\nforeground catch only fires when the LOCAL write fails.\n\ne2e/board-bulk-delete.spec.ts covers the batch, select-all skipping main,\nselection surviving a filter, cancel keeping both boards and selection, and the\nsingle-row path still behaving. Four of the five fail before this change; the\nfifth is the regression guard that must pass either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9b0a997f54a8dc27165c3ac974796a86342f324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/c9b0a997f54a8dc27165c3ac974796a86342f324"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5","verification":{"payload":"tree c9b0a997f54a8dc27165c3ac974796a86342f324\nparent 6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789534370 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789534404 -0700\n\nfeat(boards): select several boards and delete them in one confirmation\n\nPer-board confirmations are what sent a user to Chrome''s \"prevent this page\nfrom creating additional dialogs\" checkbox in the first place, which then made\nevery delete a silent no-op. The previous two commits made the dialog ours so\nit cannot be switched off; this removes the reason to want it switched off.\n\nRows in Edit Boards get a checkbox, with a select-all and a bulk bar per group.\nThe bar''s verb comes from the row''s own action — owned boards delete, boards\nshared with you leave — so a selection can never mean two different things at\nonce, and `main`, which has no destructive action, has no checkbox.\n\nOne confirmation for the batch, naming every board it will destroy: a bulk\nconfirm that only says \"3 boards\" asks the user to trust a count they cannot\ncheck, and the batch is irreversible. Six names, then a count.\n\nThe single-row button routes through the same path with a one-board list, so\nthere is one confirm, one executor and one reporter rather than a batch path\nthat drifts from the single path.\n\nDetails that are load-bearing:\n\n- Selection is keyed by board ID. The list re-sorts on pin and re-filters on\n  search; a selection addressed by position would follow whichever row moved\n  into the slot.\n- A selection survives filtering, and the bar says how many selected rows the\n  search is hiding — a count that disagrees with the screen reads as a bug.\n- The bar stays rendered whenever anything is selected, even when the filter\n  leaves fewer than two rows, or the only control that can act on or clear the\n  selection would vanish and strand it.\n- The batch runs SEQUENTIALLY and keeps going past a failure. Each delete ends\n  in a reload and those share a sequence guard that discards superseded\n  results, so concurrent deletes would let timing pick the winner. Boards that\n  fail stay checked and are named in an error toast; the rest are cleared.\n\nUnification, same commit: ClearTagModal is deleted and folded into\nConfirmModal. It was a bespoke component for a destructive confirm, which is\nwhat ConfirmModal now is for every other one.\n\nCLAUDE.md gets the rule: no alert/confirm/prompt (eslint enforces it), what to\nuse instead for each kind of message, and the detail that catches people out —\nevery write is optimistic, so a server refusal goes to onSyncError and the\nforeground catch only fires when the LOCAL write fails.\n\ne2e/board-bulk-delete.spec.ts covers the batch, select-all skipping main,\nselection surviving a filter, cancel keeping both boards and selection, and the\nsingle-row path still behaving. Four of the five fail before this change; the\nfifth is the regression guard that must pass either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOkWxYMcX/OxLslmu9BJ4JXzngZvp09wGVHo6lZWEI1vgSUgRo2o6l4cxevtaENljV\nzeOi274ARTBIrjLqd2qgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T04:53:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGQ4MDU0ZTU1YzhiYzE1ZTU1ODNlNzhhMDhjN2JmYTE3NTNiYjk3ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4","sha":"6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4"}],"sha":"d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/d8054e55c8bc15e5583e78a08c7bfa1753bb97f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T22:36:09Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T22:36:09Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(errors): report failures as toasts, and ban the dialogs that can be switched off\n\nTen `alert()` call sites reported foreground failures — a create, complete,\ndelete, reschedule, tag edit, board move or drop that the user was waiting on.\nA browser told to \"prevent this page from creating additional dialogs\" returns\nfrom alert() without drawing anything, so on the one setting a frustrated user\nis most likely to have ticked, every one of those failures reported itself to\nnobody: the card just didn''t appear and nothing explained why. One of them had\nalready been given up on in a comment — \"Note: alert() may also be blocked -\nlog instead\" — leaving that path with no user-facing report at all.\n\nuseTasks and useDragAndDrop now take an injected `onError`, which App wires to\nan error toast, matching how onSyncError already reports background failures.\nThe toast carries the error''s own message, so a full quota reads differently\nfrom a refused write.\n\nTwo of the alerts were unreachable: BoardButton and TagContextMenu wrap calls\nthat report and resolve rather than throw, so their catch blocks never ran.\nThey keep a defensive log and lose the dialog.\n\n`addTagToTask` is deleted. It held the last `prompt()` — which fails the same\nway, returning null and silently doing nothing — and it had no call site\nanywhere in the repo.\n\nThe theme editor''s Reset All confirmed through `confirm()`, so the same setting\nturned it into a dead button. It asks with click-again-to-confirm now.\n\n`no-alert` is an eslint ERROR, so this cannot come back. CI runs lint, which is\nthe gate that would have caught the original board-delete bug. It is also what\nfound the theme editor''s call site.\n\ne2e/error-reporting.spec.ts drives the real failure these paths see. Every\nwrite is optimistic, so a server refusal goes to onSyncError; the foreground\ncatch fires when the LOCAL write fails — a full quota or blocked site data. The\nspec breaks the task blob''s write, runs with dialogs neutered, and asserts a\ntoast carrying the real reason plus no native dialog. Both reporting specs fail\non the pre-fix code; the third is a control proving a healthy board stays quiet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c4cb295549054efae9cfa90e123cd9b868391489","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/c4cb295549054efae9cfa90e123cd9b868391489"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4","verification":{"payload":"tree c4cb295549054efae9cfa90e123cd9b868391489\nparent aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789511769 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789511769 -0700\n\nfix(errors): report failures as toasts, and ban the dialogs that can be switched off\n\nTen `alert()` call sites reported foreground failures — a create, complete,\ndelete, reschedule, tag edit, board move or drop that the user was waiting on.\nA browser told to \"prevent this page from creating additional dialogs\" returns\nfrom alert() without drawing anything, so on the one setting a frustrated user\nis most likely to have ticked, every one of those failures reported itself to\nnobody: the card just didn''t appear and nothing explained why. One of them had\nalready been given up on in a comment — \"Note: alert() may also be blocked -\nlog instead\" — leaving that path with no user-facing report at all.\n\nuseTasks and useDragAndDrop now take an injected `onError`, which App wires to\nan error toast, matching how onSyncError already reports background failures.\nThe toast carries the error''s own message, so a full quota reads differently\nfrom a refused write.\n\nTwo of the alerts were unreachable: BoardButton and TagContextMenu wrap calls\nthat report and resolve rather than throw, so their catch blocks never ran.\nThey keep a defensive log and lose the dialog.\n\n`addTagToTask` is deleted. It held the last `prompt()` — which fails the same\nway, returning null and silently doing nothing — and it had no call site\nanywhere in the repo.\n\nThe theme editor''s Reset All confirmed through `confirm()`, so the same setting\nturned it into a dead button. It asks with click-again-to-confirm now.\n\n`no-alert` is an eslint ERROR, so this cannot come back. CI runs lint, which is\nthe gate that would have caught the original board-delete bug. It is also what\nfound the theme editor''s call site.\n\ne2e/error-reporting.spec.ts drives the real failure these paths see. Every\nwrite is optimistic, so a server refusal goes to onSyncError; the foreground\ncatch fires when the LOCAL write fails — a full quota or blocked site data. The\nspec breaks the task blob''s write, runs with dialogs neutered, and asserts a\ntoast carrying the real reason plus no native dialog. Both reporting specs fail\non the pre-fix code; the third is a control proving a healthy board stays quiet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKw3WTQAZOYCI+6gc2dmIAVMtVneKQ7fvcvSG8su5qp2V2fP+FOac0zWXsNyYV9f/i\n4saGif8hmo1aPKuauW+wA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T22:36:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDY0NTRiNWQ4ODk0NDI1ZTkyOWI5M2MyMWFiZTVkZjVjZWMwZWM1ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","sha":"aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8"}],"sha":"6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6454b5d8894425e929b93c21abe5df5cec0ec5f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:54:06Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:54:06Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore(release): @wolffm/themes@5.8.4 @wolffm/task@5.12.2 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"2259d831a2af3099dad7071615e12cf898de39d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/2259d831a2af3099dad7071615e12cf898de39d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGFlYTI2MDg4YzNjNmU1NzllY2ZhZDdjOTIwMWNiOTRlYmRiNzQ4Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f","sha":"6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f"}],"sha":"aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/aea26088c3c6e579ecfad7c9201cb94ebdb748c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:51:16Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:52:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(boards): delete a board without asking the browser for a dialog\n\nEvery destructive board action was guarded by `if (window.confirm(...))`.\nChrome''s \"prevent this page from creating additional dialogs\" checkbox — which\nit offers after a couple of dialogs in a row, i.e. exactly to someone deleting\nseveral boards — makes every later confirm() return `false` and render nothing.\nThe guard then fails closed permanently: Delete stays clickable, fires no\nrequest, shows nothing, logs nothing, and the only way out is clearing the\nsite''s settings in Chrome. Same trap on Leave shared board and Deactivate\nautomation, and on the alert() that reported a failed delete.\n\nReplaces all four with ConfirmModal, an in-app dialog built on the Modal the\napp already uses for ClearTagModal. Nothing user-facing is now routed through a\ndialog the browser can switch off.\n\nModal''s Escape handler becomes stack-aware: only the top-most open dialog\nanswers. Both listeners are live when a confirm sits inside Edit Boards, so one\nkeypress used to close both and drop the user out of the board list on every\ncancelled delete.\n\ne2e/board-delete-confirm.spec.ts runs with confirm/alert/prompt neutered the way\nthe browser neuters them, and fails the test if a native dialog is raised at\nall. All five specs fail on the pre-fix code.\n\nAlso fixes two things the new spec run surfaced:\n\n- preset-update.spec.ts granted a share with `userId`, which the wire dropped\n  when resolveGrantee lost its unlooked-up branch (R5). It has been a 400 ever\n  since; CI does not run Playwright, so nothing said so. Grants by name now.\n- the dev stack bound no SESSIONS_KV, so every identity resolution answered\n  NO_REGISTRY and sharing by name was unreachable locally — pure dev/prod\n  divergence. Seeds a registry with the dev user and the `X-Dev-As: other-uid`\n  counterpart, and teaches the KV fake to honour `prefix` on list().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"672aedc3a9884810640e364278852c101e99aa88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/672aedc3a9884810640e364278852c101e99aa88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f","verification":{"payload":"tree 672aedc3a9884810640e364278852c101e99aa88\nparent cc65318d393ee6ef66787ca9adc9fadbf32424b4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789505476 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789505527 -0700\n\nfix(boards): delete a board without asking the browser for a dialog\n\nEvery destructive board action was guarded by `if (window.confirm(...))`.\nChrome''s \"prevent this page from creating additional dialogs\" checkbox — which\nit offers after a couple of dialogs in a row, i.e. exactly to someone deleting\nseveral boards — makes every later confirm() return `false` and render nothing.\nThe guard then fails closed permanently: Delete stays clickable, fires no\nrequest, shows nothing, logs nothing, and the only way out is clearing the\nsite''s settings in Chrome. Same trap on Leave shared board and Deactivate\nautomation, and on the alert() that reported a failed delete.\n\nReplaces all four with ConfirmModal, an in-app dialog built on the Modal the\napp already uses for ClearTagModal. Nothing user-facing is now routed through a\ndialog the browser can switch off.\n\nModal''s Escape handler becomes stack-aware: only the top-most open dialog\nanswers. Both listeners are live when a confirm sits inside Edit Boards, so one\nkeypress used to close both and drop the user out of the board list on every\ncancelled delete.\n\ne2e/board-delete-confirm.spec.ts runs with confirm/alert/prompt neutered the way\nthe browser neuters them, and fails the test if a native dialog is raised at\nall. All five specs fail on the pre-fix code.\n\nAlso fixes two things the new spec run surfaced:\n\n- preset-update.spec.ts granted a share with `userId`, which the wire dropped\n  when resolveGrantee lost its unlooked-up branch (R5). It has been a 400 ever\n  since; CI does not run Playwright, so nothing said so. Grants by name now.\n- the dev stack bound no SESSIONS_KV, so every identity resolution answered\n  NO_REGISTRY and sharing by name was unreachable locally — pure dev/prod\n  divergence. Seeds a registry with the dev user and the `X-Dev-As: other-uid`\n  counterpart, and teaches the KV fake to honour `prefix` on list().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBB8hAhHk8FCk0mqJmleCcoPTtWh+lYAZKY1M848dHUutvPOETE6+OSQEO8whUDj78\nUuIk2H/kyrJETfimICGQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T20:52:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDYwNzY2OTFhMzk2ZmJhYzg5Njc5NTg5YmI1ZmRkMTkxODllZTljMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/cc65318d393ee6ef66787ca9adc9fadbf32424b4","sha":"cc65318d393ee6ef66787ca9adc9fadbf32424b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/cc65318d393ee6ef66787ca9adc9fadbf32424b4"}],"sha":"6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6076691a396fbac89679589bb5fdd19189ee9c1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/cc65318d393ee6ef66787ca9adc9fadbf32424b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:42:27Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T20:43:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(notes): a bare URL in the notes is a link you can follow\n\nContact''s mirrored bookings put the meeting join link in the task''s notes, and\nthe notes renderer supports no link syntax at all — so the link arrived as\nplain text you had to select and copy.\n\n`renderInline` now turns a bare http(s) URL into an <a>. The URL pattern is the\nwhole allowlist: no other scheme can match, so `javascript:` never reaches an\nhref, and `[text](url)` stays unsupported rather than opening a second way to\nput an arbitrary string there. Trailing sentence punctuation is trimmed off the\nhref and still rendered, so \"see https://example.com/a.\" links the URL and\nkeeps the full stop.\n\nThe affordance is the underline, not a hue — there is no preflight here so the\nUA blue would leak through, and --color-primary is a fill colour that fails AA\nas bare text on a card (check-usage says so, which is how the first attempt at\nthis got caught). Hover moves to the validated primary tint pair.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3042cf2d82ae58b5c9f6dc6ae4c238aff15237b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/3042cf2d82ae58b5c9f6dc6ae4c238aff15237b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/cc65318d393ee6ef66787ca9adc9fadbf32424b4","verification":{"payload":"tree 3042cf2d82ae58b5c9f6dc6ae4c238aff15237b4\nparent b0f9f5bf917d55fcf41b3f1f9abe6d2bf3c7e80f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789504947 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789504981 -0700\n\nfeat(notes): a bare URL in the notes is a link you can follow\n\nContact''s mirrored bookings put the meeting join link in the task''s notes, and\nthe notes renderer supports no link syntax at all — so the link arrived as\nplain text you had to select and copy.\n\n`renderInline` now turns a bare http(s) URL into an <a>. The URL pattern is the\nwhole allowlist: no other scheme can match, so `javascript:` never reaches an\nhref, and `[text](url)` stays unsupported rather than opening a second way to\nput an arbitrary string there. Trailing sentence punctuation is trimmed off the\nhref and still rendered, so \"see https://example.com/a.\" links the URL and\nkeeps the full stop.\n\nThe affordance is the underline, not a hue — there is no preflight here so the\nUA blue would leak through, and --color-primary is a fill colour that fails AA\nas bare text on a card (check-usage says so, which is how the first attempt at\nthis got caught). Hover moves to the validated primary tint pair.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJhFoaq6CvYHGAVeUVuhkKY8DJvS/2O7PuLs7LfSqYvofnj7tGHT+vACpzRq0MLFiW\nRtRxJW5O94Y9AiANyqMgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T20:43:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"