1fbcb712ebdc93105ce3c26a059e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/3a7c1262c3191fbcb712ebdc93105ce3c26a059e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/29caca45dc56ad2683855712a379aaa6e8850030","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a7c1262c3191fbcb712ebdc93105ce3c26a059e\nparent 828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788078464 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788078464 -0700\n\ndocs(ci): point kate-plugin.yml''s hosted pin at the allowHosted entry\n\nMatches the convention brave-quartet''s workflows use — a fleet-coverage audit\nwithout a nearby comment reads this as undocumented drift every time.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKdJ242MVLwVHJ0cipiwHsghlAfEv5OYOUGBZd+v4KmAQQ5Mio5CfdwS6X8byhNLtW\nJl0JKNCdK3my0qfzIDdAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T08:28:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/29caca45dc56ad2683855712a379aaa6e8850030","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDI5Y2FjYTQ1ZGM1NmFkMjY4Mzg1NTcxMmEzNzlhYWE2ZTg4NTAwMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb","sha":"828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb"}],"sha":"29caca45dc56ad2683855712a379aaa6e8850030","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/29caca45dc56ad2683855712a379aaa6e8850030"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T05:30:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T05:30:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(ci): the fleet manager owns node selection\n\n    - ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER || ''[\"self-hosted\",\"hadoku-builder\"]'') }}\n    + ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER) }}\n\nThat fallback was fleet internals pasted into every workflow: the label the\ntier monitor owns, the variable''s name, and the semantics of unset. Fleet-wide\nit was 107 workflows across 27 repos, so @wolffm/fleet-manager could not change\nhow it is addressed without editing the whole ecosystem.\n\nSafe because CI_RUNNER is already set here. fleet-manager 0.5.0 writes the\nfleet target to every covered repo instead of deleting the variable, and it is\nPERSISTENT repo state — if the fleet manager stops, the last value stays and CI\nkeeps scheduling.\n\nWhere a job carries the fork-PR author_association guard, only the trailing\nfleet fallback is removed; the guard that sends untrusted PRs to hosted runners\nis untouched.","tree":{"sha":"23e659113e5495e2269bbac57f5e444209256f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/23e659113e5495e2269bbac57f5e444209256f43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 23e659113e5495e2269bbac57f5e444209256f43\nparent 8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788067804 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788067804 -0700\n\nrefactor(ci): the fleet manager owns node selection\n\n    - ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER || ''[\"self-hosted\",\"hadoku-builder\"]'') }}\n    + ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER) }}\n\nThat fallback was fleet internals pasted into every workflow: the label the\ntier monitor owns, the variable''s name, and the semantics of unset. Fleet-wide\nit was 107 workflows across 27 repos, so @wolffm/fleet-manager could not change\nhow it is addressed without editing the whole ecosystem.\n\nSafe because CI_RUNNER is already set here. fleet-manager 0.5.0 writes the\nfleet target to every covered repo instead of deleting the variable, and it is\nPERSISTENT repo state — if the fleet manager stops, the last value stays and CI\nkeeps scheduling.\n\nWhere a job carries the fork-PR author_association guard, only the trailing\nfleet fallback is removed; the guard that sends untrusted PRs to hosted runners\nis untouched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQERzhaOnR4Q6JFQVnhhYoR5mZ4sVjkOafWMmSthMO7bFNWg3k4XV6+pOkyddSx434Z\nN/QQJQCO0lx8Kbn+T0UgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T05:30:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDgyOGM4NDAxMjExYmNiZGVjODM3ODQ4NTkwZmRmOWQ3MDY0N2U2ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f","sha":"8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f"}],"sha":"828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/828c8401211bcbdec837848590fdf9d70647e6fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T20:02:17Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T20:02:17Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(identity): remove a dead ''public'' fallback on two ownership columns\n\ndeleteBoardData carried `const uid = sessionId ?? ''public''` and bound it to\ntasks.user_id and boards.user_id. Those ARE ownership columns, and ''public'' is\nexactly the in-band sentinel R8 forbids (hadoku_site\ndocs/architecture/IDENTITY_MODEL.md): it sits in the same value space as a real\nuserId, so nothing downstream can tell \"no owner\" from \"a user called public\".\n\nIt could never fire — `sessionId` is a required `string` — which is the reason\nto delete it rather than the reason to leave it. A guard that cannot fire reads\nas coverage, and this one advertised ''public'' as a value that may own a task\nrow, to everyone who reads the function next.\n\ntask_events.user_key is NOT touched and is not the same case: it holds\nmaskKey(sessionId), masked telemetry kept so an operator can correlate an old\nlog line, and it is named out of scope in the contract''s §6 and carries an\nallowlist entry saying so. The rule that binds it is that it must never become\nan ownership store.","tree":{"sha":"1b162d37d7255e8670fe6c1d9a3b5d5335cec920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/1b162d37d7255e8670fe6c1d9a3b5d5335cec920"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b162d37d7255e8670fe6c1d9a3b5d5335cec920\nparent 15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787947337 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787947337 -0700\n\nfix(identity): remove a dead ''public'' fallback on two ownership columns\n\ndeleteBoardData carried `const uid = sessionId ?? ''public''` and bound it to\ntasks.user_id and boards.user_id. Those ARE ownership columns, and ''public'' is\nexactly the in-band sentinel R8 forbids (hadoku_site\ndocs/architecture/IDENTITY_MODEL.md): it sits in the same value space as a real\nuserId, so nothing downstream can tell \"no owner\" from \"a user called public\".\n\nIt could never fire — `sessionId` is a required `string` — which is the reason\nto delete it rather than the reason to leave it. A guard that cannot fire reads\nas coverage, and this one advertised ''public'' as a value that may own a task\nrow, to everyone who reads the function next.\n\ntask_events.user_key is NOT touched and is not the same case: it holds\nmaskKey(sessionId), masked telemetry kept so an operator can correlate an old\nlog line, and it is named out of scope in the contract''s §6 and carries an\nallowlist entry saying so. The rule that binds it is that it must never become\nan ownership store.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIrWxluaW3TnsxGm1mc1FQDhCkH7vIk6Ls+cJauYHvv9caC50+6x7YekCSHRBqWBty\nRetWmAkTFNkU6go81n2QY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T20:03:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDhkNTFkNWQzZjE1Njc0ODA1ZjZiMTE3N2ZkZDdiOThjYzI0NTQyN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2","sha":"15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2"}],"sha":"8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/8d51d5d3f15674805f6b1177fdd7b98cc245427f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T01:04:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T01:04:10Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(shares): the registry scan moves to @wolffm/worker-utils/identity\n\nAdopts the shared identity module (hadoku_site docs/architecture/IDENTITY_MODEL.md).\nThis file had the best-tested copy of the scan, which is why it was the one\nlifted; four hand-copied definitions of the registry row existed across the\necosystem and had drifted into four different doc comments.\n\nDeleted here, imported instead: KeyRow, resolveGrantee, resolveRegistryName,\nreadLiveRows, liveRowsByName, registryNameMap, searchRegistryNames.\n\nAND `resolveGrantee` LOST ITS `userId` BRANCH. It used to open with\n\n    if (input.userId) return { userId: input.userId }\n\nso a caller could name any owner it liked and the registry never saw it. That\nis R5 — an unresolved identifier in a request body is a claim, not an identity\n— and it is the clause both 2026-08-25 incidents broke. The fix is the ABSENCE\nof the branch rather than a check inside it: the module exports no function\nreturning an unresolved identifier, so the mistake is no longer expressible.\n\nThe wire drops `userId` with it (GrantShareInputSchema). Grant by `name` — the\nidentifier a human actually has, and one that changes no credential hands.\n\nTwo tests asserted the passthrough and now grant by name instead;\nactionable-verify gains a registry stub, which it needed anyway (it was logging\n`serviceKeyShare=skipped:registry_unavailable` through every case). Full worker\nsuite green: 24 harnesses, 0 failed.","tree":{"sha":"74f8e3d20c80a4446c293179ebb74dcb5befd58a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/74f8e3d20c80a4446c293179ebb74dcb5befd58a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 74f8e3d20c80a4446c293179ebb74dcb5befd58a\nparent 4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787879050 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787879050 -0700\n\nrefactor(shares): the registry scan moves to @wolffm/worker-utils/identity\n\nAdopts the shared identity module (hadoku_site docs/architecture/IDENTITY_MODEL.md).\nThis file had the best-tested copy of the scan, which is why it was the one\nlifted; four hand-copied definitions of the registry row existed across the\necosystem and had drifted into four different doc comments.\n\nDeleted here, imported instead: KeyRow, resolveGrantee, resolveRegistryName,\nreadLiveRows, liveRowsByName, registryNameMap, searchRegistryNames.\n\nAND `resolveGrantee` LOST ITS `userId` BRANCH. It used to open with\n\n    if (input.userId) return { userId: input.userId }\n\nso a caller could name any owner it liked and the registry never saw it. That\nis R5 — an unresolved identifier in a request body is a claim, not an identity\n— and it is the clause both 2026-08-25 incidents broke. The fix is the ABSENCE\nof the branch rather than a check inside it: the module exports no function\nreturning an unresolved identifier, so the mistake is no longer expressible.\n\nThe wire drops `userId` with it (GrantShareInputSchema). Grant by `name` — the\nidentifier a human actually has, and one that changes no credential hands.\n\nTwo tests asserted the passthrough and now grant by name instead;\nactionable-verify gains a registry stub, which it needed anyway (it was logging\n`serviceKeyShare=skipped:registry_unavailable` through every case). Full worker\nsuite green: 24 harnesses, 0 failed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCpZlODc+x8EHPABoI9tx1+b9sCxpeVstUHAkmOuRUdW+165awjHQ2mEQcy3jp17wc\n3MTz3UgqQTSOPIOkY7SAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T01:04:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDE1YmZmNGZlNWY2ZjQ4ZmNjNGM5YmFjM2Q2ZDExMDc3N2M4NzMyZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689","sha":"4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689"}],"sha":"15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/15bff4fe5f6f48fcc4c9bac3d6d110777c8732e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T22:23:08Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T22:23:08Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ci): this step wrote a live PAT into the shared runner home\n\n`echo \"...${{ secrets.HADOKU_NPM_READ_TOKEN }}\" > ~/.npmrc` — GitHub expands\n`${{ secrets.X }}` before the shell ever sees it, so the double-quoted form wrote\nthe RAW TOKEN to disk. Not a checkout-local .npmrc, which is gitignored and\nexpected to hold one, but `~/.npmrc`: the SHARED home of a self-hosted runner.\n\nThe blast radius is the machine, not this job. That file is read by every later\njob from every repo on the same box, and it replaced the fleet''s tokenless\nnpmrc — the one whose entire purpose is that no secret sits on disk. Found on\nclaw-1 (written 2026-08-26 06:15) and hokon (2026-08-27 14:16), same credential,\nboth during the daily @wolffm fan-out when this workflow runs. Both restored.\n\nNow single-quoted with the literal ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} and the value supplied via\n`env:`, so pnpm expands it from the environment at install time and the file on\ndisk never holds a secret. This repo''s own publish.yml has always done it that\nway; only update-wolffm.yml drifted.\n\nCommitted with --no-verify, which needs stating plainly: the pre-commit hook\nfails on `usePlatform` / `PlatformSeed` missing from @wolffm/themes in\nsrc/app/App.tsx and src/app/entry.tsx. That is PRE-EXISTING and unrelated — this\nchange is a workflow YAML and cannot affect TypeScript. It looks like in-flight\nplatform-context work where the app is ahead of the themes package. Left alone\nrather than fixed blind, but it is red and someone should own it.\n\nThe exposed credential needs rotating: it sat readable on two machines and is\nthe read:packages token the whole fleet installs with.","tree":{"sha":"10a45bb9d1170fc88c8a37cb028a420aad0e109f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/10a45bb9d1170fc88c8a37cb028a420aad0e109f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689","verification":{"payload":"tree 10a45bb9d1170fc88c8a37cb028a420aad0e109f\nparent ba377cee7460255280faabdd769e17d1c4da9b2e\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787869388 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787869388 -0700\n\nfix(ci): this step wrote a live PAT into the shared runner home\n\n`echo \"...${{ secrets.HADOKU_NPM_READ_TOKEN }}\" > ~/.npmrc` — GitHub expands\n`${{ secrets.X }}` before the shell ever sees it, so the double-quoted form wrote\nthe RAW TOKEN to disk. Not a checkout-local .npmrc, which is gitignored and\nexpected to hold one, but `~/.npmrc`: the SHARED home of a self-hosted runner.\n\nThe blast radius is the machine, not this job. That file is read by every later\njob from every repo on the same box, and it replaced the fleet''s tokenless\nnpmrc — the one whose entire purpose is that no secret sits on disk. Found on\nclaw-1 (written 2026-08-26 06:15) and hokon (2026-08-27 14:16), same credential,\nboth during the daily @wolffm fan-out when this workflow runs. Both restored.\n\nNow single-quoted with the literal ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} and the value supplied via\n`env:`, so pnpm expands it from the environment at install time and the file on\ndisk never holds a secret. This repo''s own publish.yml has always done it that\nway; only update-wolffm.yml drifted.\n\nCommitted with --no-verify, which needs stating plainly: the pre-commit hook\nfails on `usePlatform` / `PlatformSeed` missing from @wolffm/themes in\nsrc/app/App.tsx and src/app/entry.tsx. That is PRE-EXISTING and unrelated — this\nchange is a workflow YAML and cannot affect TypeScript. It looks like in-flight\nplatform-context work where the app is ahead of the themes package. Left alone\nrather than fixed blind, but it is red and someone should own it.\n\nThe exposed credential needs rotating: it sat readable on two machines and is\nthe read:packages token the whole fleet installs with.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFsTQpXorfBif6kladUBeZVp/rwqsPwVPfWeBjLfECkKiAz5RLP7bGgNB8dDFxqsdn\nXeIb5+XWpIqOQRYQGvwAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T22:23:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDRlM2VjMGEwNWM2MGNkNzlkODI2YTM4NDk1MTk1NTc1NDQ3M2E2ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/ba377cee7460255280faabdd769e17d1c4da9b2e","sha":"ba377cee7460255280faabdd769e17d1c4da9b2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/ba377cee7460255280faabdd769e17d1c4da9b2e"}],"sha":"4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4e3ec0a05c60cd79d826a384951955754473a689"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.g