ps://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/5b74480b05366fb34b7596a4b66d7680285ff7bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:52:03Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T20:52:44Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(themes): one platform definition for the fleet, replacing six\n\nSix independent isMobile implementations across the ecosystem, four different\nthresholds (768, 820, 900, 1000), answering three different questions. Two\ndisagreed with their own CSS: pygmalion branched on `innerWidth >= 900` while\nits stylesheet carried max-width 900px, 899px AND 820px — so at exactly 900px\nthe JS said desktop and the CSS said mobile — and dataplatform ran a pure\npointer query in JS against twelve `max-width:900px` rules, giving a landscape\ntablet touch-first behaviour and desktop layout simultaneously.\n\nSame failure as the eight hand-copied useTheme.ts files this package already\nabsorbed, so it takes the same shape: the host passes a seed on mount and a\nshared hook owns the live value.\n\nTwo flags, deliberately, with no `isMobile` OR convenience. `touchFirst`\n(pointer:coarse and hover:none) and `narrow` (max-width:767px) are different\nquestions — a phone in landscape is touch-first but not narrow, a small desktop\nwindow is narrow but not touch-first — and a single boolean would become the\ndefault reach and put the fleet back on one blessed threshold under a new name.\n\n`propsPlatform` is a SEED, not an override like propsTheme: host and app are in\nthe same document looking at the same viewport, so the host has no privileged\nknowledge. The media queries take over from the first effect, which is what\nkeeps a rotation from being lost. The effect resyncs once on mount for the same\nreason — the host computes the seed at DOMContentLoaded and the bundle is\nimported dynamically after, so a change inside that window fires before anything\nis listening. Bailing out via the setState updater when nothing moved makes that\nrepair free.\n\nstampPlatform mirrors the flags as data-touch-first / data-narrow so CSS keys\noff the identical source the JS does, which is what makes the two JS/CSS\ndisagreements above impossible to reintroduce.\n\nFramework-free half at @wolffm/themes/platform for the plain-TS consumers\n(merchant), React hook at ./platform/react — same split as ./icons.\n\nVerified behaviourally against the built dist with a driven MediaQueryList\nstub: query strings, detection, store attach/detach on first/last subscribe,\nchange propagation, no spurious notify on an identical value, seed repair for a\nchange missed before subscribe, attribute stamping and clearing, and the\nno-matchMedia environment. That last case caught a real ordering bug —\nsubscribe() attached (and ran its repair sync) before adding the listener, so a\nnew subscriber missed the very change the resync exists to surface.","tree":{"sha":"fee6bd8c104f90e4142e2d57455b64aefd4bd29c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/fee6bd8c104f90e4142e2d57455b64aefd4bd29c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/5b74480b05366fb34b7596a4b66d7680285ff7bb","verification":{"payload":"tree fee6bd8c104f90e4142e2d57455b64aefd4bd29c\nparent 8d1334dd8fa59350bff95cc2bf9a9223a3cf8b69\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787691123 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787691164 -0700\n\nfeat(themes): one platform definition for the fleet, replacing six\n\nSix independent isMobile implementations across the ecosystem, four different\nthresholds (768, 820, 900, 1000), answering three different questions. Two\ndisagreed with their own CSS: pygmalion branched on `innerWidth >= 900` while\nits stylesheet carried max-width 900px, 899px AND 820px — so at exactly 900px\nthe JS said desktop and the CSS said mobile — and dataplatform ran a pure\npointer query in JS against twelve `max-width:900px` rules, giving a landscape\ntablet touch-first behaviour and desktop layout simultaneously.\n\nSame failure as the eight hand-copied useTheme.ts files this package already\nabsorbed, so it takes the same shape: the host passes a seed on mount and a\nshared hook owns the live value.\n\nTwo flags, deliberately, with no `isMobile` OR convenience. `touchFirst`\n(pointer:coarse and hover:none) and `narrow` (max-width:767px) are different\nquestions — a phone in landscape is touch-first but not narrow, a small desktop\nwindow is narrow but not touch-first — and a single boolean would become the\ndefault reach and put the fleet back on one blessed threshold under a new name.\n\n`propsPlatform` is a SEED, not an override like propsTheme: host and app are in\nthe same document looking at the same viewport, so the host has no privileged\nknowledge. The media queries take over from the first effect, which is what\nkeeps a rotation from being lost. The effect resyncs once on mount for the same\nreason — the host computes the seed at DOMContentLoaded and the bundle is\nimported dynamically after, so a change inside that window fires before anything\nis listening. Bailing out via the setState updater when nothing moved makes that\nrepair free.\n\nstampPlatform mirrors the flags as data-touch-first / data-narrow so CSS keys\noff the identical source the JS does, which is what makes the two JS/CSS\ndisagreements above impossible to reintroduce.\n\nFramework-free half at @wolffm/themes/platform for the plain-TS consumers\n(merchant), React hook at ./platform/react — same split as ./icons.\n\nVerified behaviourally against the built dist with a driven MediaQueryList\nstub: query strings, detection, store attach/detach on first/last subscribe,\nchange propagation, no spurious notify on an identical value, seed repair for a\nchange missed before subscribe, attribute stamping and clearing, and the\nno-matchMedia environment. That last case caught a real ordering bug —\nsubscribe() attached (and ran its repair sync) before adding the listener, so a\nnew subscriber missed the very change the resync exists to surface.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF4HpCFBCEYIf1oPN7FRWc1nLDdAIpFUhkqjNHGvr0SrN4FCVpqbpCDsNOGdg+agsh\nzna23tf1Xxfd45qwL1NAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T20:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://a