me minute\n\nEvery repo carrying this workflow ran `cron: \"0 6 * * *\"`, so all eleven fanned\nout at the SAME minute onto claws that each share ONE pnpm store across ~28\nrunner instances. That is a synchronised thundering herd against a single\nmutable resource, every day.\n\nIt is not theoretical. Tonight concurrent installs corrupted the pnpm stores on\ntwo claws — truncated zero-byte content files on claw-3, and a store index that\nmapped yauzl@2.10.0 to body-parser@1.20.6 on claw-2. pnpm''s\nstrictStorePkgContentCheck is the only reason that surfaced as a loud failure\nrather than silently installing one package''s code under another''s name. It took\nhadoku_site''s CI down for about an hour across three workflows.\n\n`workflow_dispatch` is kept, so the audit still runs on demand from the Actions\ntab. Nothing about vibeCompact itself is wrong — the schedule''s shape is.\n\nIf this is restored, give each repo a DIFFERENT minute instead of putting the\nline back verbatim; the comment left in place says so.","tree":{"sha":"554074337ee957b57cad26a41c076847435c0c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/554074337ee957b57cad26a41c076847435c0c76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/65172e68c2ae31afba9c3ead7570db247c3ead65","verification":{"payload":"tree 554074337ee957b57cad26a41c076847435c0c76\nparent 12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787639268 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787639268 -0700\n\nci(vibecompact): disable the daily cron — 11 repos fired the same minute\n\nEvery repo carrying this workflow ran `cron: \"0 6 * * *\"`, so all eleven fanned\nout at the SAME minute onto claws that each share ONE pnpm store across ~28\nrunner instances. That is a synchronised thundering herd against a single\nmutable resource, every day.\n\nIt is not theoretical. Tonight concurrent installs corrupted the pnpm stores on\ntwo claws — truncated zero-byte content files on claw-3, and a store index that\nmapped yauzl@2.10.0 to body-parser@1.20.6 on claw-2. pnpm''s\nstrictStorePkgContentCheck is the only reason that surfaced as a loud failure\nrather than silently installing one package''s code under another''s name. It took\nhadoku_site''s CI down for about an hour across three workflows.\n\n`workflow_dispatch` is kept, so the audit still runs on demand from the Actions\ntab. Nothing about vibeCompact itself is wrong — the schedule''s shape is.\n\nIf this is restored, give each repo a DIFFERENT minute instead of putting the\nline back verbatim; the comment left in place says so.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGMRgwgoHtw30XCfnMMDPK2aR5bhYZG+TdCEb3lJL4Ijj/iKR4Bh1Drf9Gte18qVxj\nz9tMoMCo9DVI+FHNagSQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T06:31:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/65172e68c2ae31afba9c3ead7570db247c3ead65","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDY1MTcyZTY4YzJhZTMxYWZiYTljM2VhZDc1NzBkYjI0N2MzZWFkNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0","sha":"12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0"}],"sha":"65172e68c2ae31afba9c3ead7570db247c3ead65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/65172e68c2ae31afba9c3ead7570db247c3ead65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T06:23:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T06:23:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(git): ignore .claude/worktrees so `git add -A` cannot commit one\n\nA worktree here is a FULL second checkout of this repo on another branch, and\nnothing was ignoring it: with one open, `git add -A --dry-run` staged it. That\nis a whole parallel tree one careless command away from being committed.\n\nSCOPED ON PURPOSE, not `.claude/`. settings.local.json is tracked here. A\nblanket ignore would leave it tracked — gitignore does not untrack — while\nsilently swallowing the NEXT file added under .claude/. `.claude/worktrees/` is\nthe fleet convention: hadoku_site, merchant, contact-ui, jobplatform,\nwatchparty, aggregator and resume-bot all carry exactly this line.\n\nThe file is also normalised CRLF -> LF, which is why the diff is 85 lines rather\nthan 6; `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` shows the real change is the 6 added ones.\nDone deliberately rather than appending LF lines into a CRLF file and leaving it\nmixed.\n\nVerified with a worktree open: `git add -A --dry-run` staged 1 path before and 0\nafter, and the tracked .claude/ file still passes `git check-ignore` untouched.","tree":{"sha":"726e7abec7db1a3f5b6caf6d617e169944985fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/726e7abec7db1a3f5b6caf6d617e169944985fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0","verification":{"payload":"tree 726e7abec7db1a3f5b6caf6d617e169944985fa6\nparent 6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787639022 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787639022 -0700\n\nchore(git): ignore .claude/worktrees so `git add -A` cannot commit one\n\nA worktree here is a FULL second checkout of this repo on another branch, and\nnothing was ignoring it: with one open, `git add -A --dry-run` staged it. That\nis a whole parallel tree one careless command away from being committed.\n\nSCOPED ON PURPOSE, not `.claude/`. settings.local.json is tracked here. A\nblanket ignore would leave it tracked — gitignore does not untrack — while\nsilently swallowing the NEXT file added under .claude/. `.claude/worktrees/` is\nthe fleet convention: hadoku_site, merchant, contact-ui, jobplatform,\nwatchparty, aggregator and resume-bot all carry exactly this line.\n\nThe file is also normalised CRLF -> LF, which is why the diff is 85 lines rather\nthan 6; `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` shows the real change is the 6 added ones.\nDone deliberately rather than appending LF lines into a CRLF file and leaving it\nmixed.\n\nVerified with a worktree open: `git add -A --dry-run` staged 1 path before and 0\nafter, and the tracked .claude/ file still passes `git check-ignore` untouched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF9JlLuzIvbeo4TZWRGtuJlVzS4U1QNDWqNVQC8pEsUHipNasKUVxtjNAgyxI91upu\n9yNGoNK72a1UV7sE3NqwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T06:31:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDEyZmYwMTAzZWQ3MTRlZTZkYjVmNDFmYjM4ODU5ZTg0YmE3N2Y4YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960","sha":"6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960"}],"sha":"12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/12ff0103ed714ee6db5f41fb38859e84ba77f8b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T03:00:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T03:00:54Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: make the worktree preamble workspace-aware\n\nThe first cut linked only the ROOT node_modules. A pnpm workspace keeps one\nper package, so any gate that shells into themes/, worker/ or frontend/\nstill failed on a missing devDependency — hadoku-task''s theme gate went down\nexactly that way, on lucide-static, in a file nobody had touched.\n\nIt now links every node_modules the main checkout has, and resolves the main\ncheckout once up front so a repo can borrow other gitignored artifacts its\ngates read on the same footing.","tree":{"sha":"36d66c2181d60cdb8eae09d1e9201f684c091618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/36d66c2181d60cdb8eae09d1e9201f684c091618"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960","verification":{"payload":"tree 36d66c2181d60cdb8eae09d1e9201f684c091618\nparent 755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787626854 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787626854 -0700\n\nfix: make the worktree preamble workspace-aware\n\nThe first cut linked only the ROOT node_modules. A pnpm workspace keeps one\nper package, so any gate that shells into themes/, worker/ or frontend/\nstill failed on a missing devDependency — hadoku-task''s theme gate went down\nexactly that way, on lucide-static, in a file nobody had touched.\n\nIt now links every node_modules the main checkout has, and resolves the main\ncheckout once up front so a repo can borrow other gitignored artifacts its\ngates read on the same footing.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOyW9u8v9OhrYPBBy+MBEpy1NKSvloLVrj5qcKXcYXNzD0kU45g2uL6ZJCqlqbeA+x\nflQ4c/+04cMGCld1AK4Ak=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T03:01:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDZmYzEzM2Y2OWE0MDg4NDgyZTI1NGU3OTMxZTIyY2FlZjkwZmE5NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7","sha":"755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7"}],"sha":"6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6fc133f69a4088482e254e7931e22caef90fa960"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T02:49:48Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T02:49:48Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix: run git hooks from a tracked directory so worktrees keep their gates\n\ncore.hooksPath pointed at .husky/_, which husky GENERATES and its own\n.gitignore excludes. git resolves a relative core.hooksPath against the\nworking tree root, and the setting lives in the shared config — so a\nlinked worktree inherited the setting but had no .husky/_ to run, and git\nexecuted no hook at all. Silently: no warning, no non-zero exit. Every\ncommit made from a worktree skipped the lint/typecheck gates and the\nversion bump.\n\n.husky/pre-commit and .husky/post-commit are tracked, so pointing straight\nat .husky is present in every worktree by construction. `prepare` sets it\ninstead of calling husky, husky comes out of devDependencies, and the hooks\nget their executable bit in the index — the generated shim used to run them\nwith `sh -e`, which covered for that.\n\nFiring the hook is only half of it: a fresh worktree has no node_modules\nand every gate needs one, so pre-commit borrows the main checkout''s. pnpm\nlays node_modules out as a symlink farm over its own .pnpm store, so a\nworktree on the same dependency set can point at it; a branch that changes\ndependencies fails loudly on the missing package instead.\n\nAlso drops the trailing slash from node_modules in .gitignore — it matches\ndirectories only, so it never matched the worktree symlink.","tree":{"sha":"87963b44842b015deaae29ddf6f2153f1e90d55b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/87963b44842b015deaae29ddf6f2153f1e90d55b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7","verification":{"payload":"tree 87963b44842b015deaae29ddf6f2153f1e90d55b\nparent c4c80a5be23eb31652446f9babd0d7179c3fb0f4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787626188 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787626188 -0700\n\nfix: run git hooks from a tracked directory so worktrees keep their gates\n\ncore.hooksPath pointed at .husky/_, which husky GENERATES and its own\n.gitignore excludes. git resolves a relative core.hooksPath against the\nworking tree root, and the setting lives in the shared config — so a\nlinked worktree inherited the setting but had no .husky/_ to run, and git\nexecuted no hook at all. Silently: no warning, no non-zero exit. Every\ncommit made from a worktree skipped the lint/typecheck gates and the\nversion bump.\n\n.husky/pre-commit and .husky/post-commit are tracked, so pointing straight\nat .husky is present in every worktree by construction. `prepare` sets it\ninstead of calling husky, husky comes out of devDependencies, and the hooks\nget their executable bit in the index — the generated shim used to run them\nwith `sh -e`, which covered for that.\n\nFiring the hook is only half of it: a fresh worktree has no node_modules\nand every gate needs one, so pre-commit borrows the main checkout''s. pnpm\nlays node_modules out as a symlink farm over its own .pnpm store, so a\nworktree on the same dependency set can point at it; a branch that changes\ndependencies fails loudly on the missing package instead.\n\nAlso drops the trailing slash from node_modules in .gitignore — it matches\ndirectories only, so it never matched the worktree symlink.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLGcHZJUkfv+8jUJlwrU9cBBi6qYTh8vkA+Lm5ue/EKgZg9227JD1Izvbhumlmx7VE\ndhRfVYBJ9tIezooXD0VQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T02:50:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDc1NWE1MzU4ZGJmZDZkMWI4ZmFhMjczZTQyNDJjYTcyYjNjMjZiYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/c4c80a5be23eb31652446f9babd0d7179c3fb0f4","sha":"c4c80a5be23eb31652446f9babd0d7179c3fb0f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/c4c80a5be23eb31652446f9babd0d7179c3fb0f4"}],"sha":"755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/755a5358dbfd6d1b8faa273e4242ca72b3c26bb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot