e lines and main.css\nat 566. Both were doing several unrelated jobs, and both already marked the\nseams with their own section comments.\n\n  main.css   736 -> 87    the app shell: container, safe-area, pull-to-refresh\n  settings.css      288   the settings popout, its toggles and live preview\n  boards-bar.css    203   controls, the pill row, drag visuals, the marquee\n  filters.css       171   the filters row and the cluster on its right\n\n  modal.css  842 -> 254   the primitives any dialog is built from\n  edit-boards.css   203   the Edit Boards dialog itself\n  automation-panel  247   the convert flow, preset picker, provider banner\n  share-panel.css   154   grantee autocomplete and the grantee rows\n\nThe modal split follows the component split from c2f4371 — SharePanel and\nAutomationPanel now have stylesheets named after them.\n\nCASCADE ORDER IS THE WHOLE RISK\n-------------------------------\nCSS has no imports to re-point and no compiler to catch a mistake; equal-\nspecificity rules are decided by order alone, so a split that reorders anything\nchanges rendering silently. style.css imports the eight files in exactly the\npositions the two originals occupied.\n\nVerified the only way that really settles it: `dist/style.css` — the artifact\nconsumers actually load — is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the pre-split build, same md5\n(21302ca5…), 104,677 bytes. Every rule in the same order with the same content.\n\nBecause the bundle strips comments, source-level documentation was checked\nseparately: all 44 comments from main.css and all 21 from modal.css are present\nin the parts, and no declaration line went missing.\n\nAlso green: stylelint, the token/contrast/usage gates (18 themes, 558 WCAG\npairs), and Playwright at 147 passed / 1 skipped — which includes the specs that\nassert real computed geometry (board pills, notes popout, edit-boards scroll).\n\nExisting files keep their own line endings; the new ones are LF, like the other\nrecent additions to this directory.","tree":{"sha":"8d69d7eaebde039bdd15e6c0f673a3a2a728785b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/8d69d7eaebde039bdd15e6c0f673a3a2a728785b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/8a00a372277f91b8d92ff82b5952ab1378eb5792","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d69d7eaebde039bdd15e6c0f673a3a2a728785b\nparent 61577751ba9bd99a6fcdc09572d30d84f9739b8f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787113381 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787113381 -0700\n\nrefactor(styles): split main.css and modal.css by what they style\n\nThe last two vibeCompact size findings: modal.css at 758 code lines and main.css\nat 566. Both were doing several unrelated jobs, and both already marked the\nseams with their own section comments.\n\n  main.css   736 -> 87    the app shell: container, safe-area, pull-to-refresh\n  settings.css      288   the settings popout, its toggles and live preview\n  boards-bar.css    203   controls, the pill row, drag visuals, the marquee\n  filters.css       171   the filters row and the cluster on its right\n\n  modal.css  842 -> 254   the primitives any dialog is built from\n  edit-boards.css   203   the Edit Boards dialog itself\n  automation-panel  247   the convert flow, preset picker, provider banner\n  share-panel.css   154   grantee autocomplete and the grantee rows\n\nThe modal split follows the component split from c2f4371 — SharePanel and\nAutomationPanel now have stylesheets named after them.\n\nCASCADE ORDER IS THE WHOLE RISK\n-------------------------------\nCSS has no imports to re-point and no compiler to catch a mistake; equal-\nspecificity rules are decided by order alone, so a split that reorders anything\nchanges rendering silently. style.css imports the eight files in exactly the\npositions the two originals occupied.\n\nVerified the only way that really settles it: `dist/style.css` — the artifact\nconsumers actually load — is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the pre-split build, same md5\n(21302ca5…), 104,677 bytes. Every rule in the same order with the same content.\n\nBecause the bundle strips comments, source-level documentation was checked\nseparately: all 44 comments from main.css and all 21 from modal.css are present\nin the parts, and no declaration line went missing.\n\nAlso green: stylelint, the token/contrast/usage gates (18 themes, 558 WCAG\npairs), and Playwright at 147 passed / 1 skipped — which includes the specs that\nassert real computed geometry (board pills, notes popout, edit-boards scroll).\n\nExisting files keep their own line endings; the new ones are LF, like the other\nrecent additions to this directory.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNpy9dfCR/oyl0vJrEBA+xtIsn9+5etRjPuzSdHu3+kdZKG7ObJFm7qrn0Txu4BYUO\nxG1jutcdDltGuy2PnQXw4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T04:24:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_