Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:52:14Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(worker): separate the share helpers from the share routes\n\nvibeCompact size finding: worker/src/routes/shares.ts at 534 code lines. Unlike\nautomation.ts the route factory was only 39% of it — the rest was helper code\nthat four OTHER modules import. That is the actual smell here: automation-repo,\nautomation-reconcile, automation-activation and boards.ts were all reaching into\na ROUTE file for grant machinery and name derivation.\n\n  shares.ts          534 -> 289   the routes, and only the routes\n  share-registry.ts         248   resolving who a grantee is, against the registry\n  share-grants.ts           193   the §7 auto-grants\n  share-naming.ts            62   the repo → service-key convention\n\nThe four importers now point at the module that owns what they want, so nothing\noutside this group imports from a route file any more.\n\nshare-naming is its own module rather than a corner of share-grants because it\nis the load-bearing convention: a registry row carries no `repo` field, so the\nNAME is the only link between a board''s checkout mapping and an identity, and\n3f240cf pins every case of it.\n\n`nowIso` sat between the slices and belongs to no one concern; it lands in\nshare-registry, the lowest-level module of the three, which grants and routes\nalready both import.\n\nPure code movement plus visibility: every line of the five moved blocks appears\nverbatim in its new home once an added `export` keyword is normalised away —\nchecked mechanically, 0 lines unaccounted for. The generated openapi.json is\nbyte-identical to origin/main''s, compared by booting the real worker.\n\nVerified: all 20 worker harnesses green — shared-boards (52) and automation\n(117) are what actually drive this code — plus Playwright 147 passed / 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"36c06e071db45fba803837f6a9e6ad562e25ca5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/36c06e071db45fba803837f6a9e6ad562e25ca5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/7344f262beafd8a624223dce5b0e120df154e935","verification":{"payload":"tree 36c06e071db45fba803837f6a9e6ad562e25ca5d\nparent 3f240cfcadd35d7a2044d79b7beb86e70944149b\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787107934 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787107934 -0700\n\nrefactor(worker): separate the share helpers from the share routes\n\nvibeCompact size finding: worker/src/routes/shares.ts at 534 code lines. Unlike\nautomation.ts the route factory was only 39% of it — the rest was helper code\nthat four OTHER modules import. That is the actual smell here: automation-repo,\nautomation-reconcile, automation-activation and boards.ts were all reaching into\na ROUTE file for grant machinery and name derivation.\n\n  shares.ts          534 -> 289   the routes, and only the routes\n  share-registry.ts         248   resolving who a grantee is, against the registry\n  share-grants.ts           193   the §7 auto-grants\n  share-naming.ts            62   the repo → service-key convention\n\nThe four importers now point at the module that owns what they want, so nothing\noutside this group imports from a route file any more.\n\nshare-naming is its own module rather than a corner of share-grants because it\nis the load-bearing convention: a registry row carries no `repo` field, so the\nNAME is the only link between a board''s checkout mapping and an identity, and\n3f240cf pins every case of it.\n\n`nowIso` sat between the slices and belongs to no one concern; it lands in\nshare-registry, the lowest-level module of the three, which grants and routes\nalready both import.\n\nPure code movement plus visibility: every line of the five moved blocks appears\nverbatim in its new home once an added `export` keyword is normalised away —\nchecked mechanically, 0 lines unaccounted for. The generated openapi.json is\nbyte-identical to origin/main''s, compared by booting the real worker.\n\nVerified: all 20 worker harnesses green — shared-boards (52) and automation\n(117) are what actually drive this code — plus Playwright 147 passed / 1 skipped.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOQ0yFYgU0fHSRFO7dC91vaecfjnT47GFVn3nE6KAahY6/yzywZRazc4miVF588acK\nG2Us1J52YlJMl903/wLQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T02:53:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/7344f262beafd8a624223dce5b0e120df154e935","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDczNDRmMjYyYmVhZmQ4YTYyNDIyM2RjZTViMGUxMjBkZjE1NGU5MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/3f240cfcadd35d7a2044d79b7beb86e70944149b","sha":"3f240cfcadd35d7a2044d79b7beb86e70944149b","url":"https://