ng and an\nidentity: the registry row carries no `repo` field, so the NAME is the whole\nmechanism, and its own doc says this derivation is \"the single place that has to\nchange\" if the convention moves.\n\nautomation-verify does reach the two cases that bit in production — hadoku_site\nspells the separator with an underscore, and a repo can arrive capitalised — but\nonly over HTTP, where a null return is indistinguishable from a grant skipped for\nsome other reason. The edges are not reachable that way at all: no repo, a\ntrailing slash, a bare `hadoku-` that would trim to nothing and resolve a garbage\nname for a share granted to nobody.\n\nAlso pins automationRunnerName, whose blank-binding fallback matters for the same\nreason.\n\nConfirmed the assertions have teeth by narrowing the prefix trim back to\nhyphen-only, which fails exactly the hadoku_site case. 19 assertions, all passing\nagainst today''s code. No production code changed.","tree":{"sha":"07ed10902b25ae91359376310dfffea86952b032","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/07ed10902b25ae91359376310dfffea86952b032"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/3f240cfcadd35d7a2044d79b7beb86e70944149b","verification":{"payload":"tree 07ed10902b25ae91359376310dfffea86952b032\nparent 2a205c52feb0415f0bd6741fe71e0e158648f3f7\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787107619 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787107619 -0700\n\ntest(worker): pin the repo → service-key naming convention\n\nvibeCompact flags worker/src/routes/shares.ts on size, and splitting it needs a\ntest first. The routes themselves are covered well — shared-boards-verify and\nautomation-verify drive them over HTTP, and `shares` appears 34 times across the\nharnesses. What had no direct assertion was the naming convention underneath.\n\n`repoServiceKeyName` is the only link between a board''s checkout mapping and an\nidentity: the registry row carries no `repo` field, so the NAME is the whole\nmechanism, and its own doc says this derivation is \"the single place that has to\nchange\" if the convention moves.\n\nautomation-verify does reach the two cases that bit in production — hadoku_site\nspells the separator with an underscore, and a repo can arrive capitalised — but\nonly over HTTP, where a null return is indistinguishable from a grant skipped for\nsome other reason. The edges are not reachable that way at all: no repo, a\ntrailing slash, a bare `hadoku-` that would trim to nothing and resolve a garbage\nname for a share granted to nobody.\n\nAlso pins automationRunnerName, whose blank-binding fallback matters for the same\nreason.\n\nConfirmed the assertions have teeth by narrowing the prefix trim back to\nhyphen-only, which fails exactly the hadoku_site case. 19 assertions, all passing\nagainst today''s code. No production code changed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHOb5XBz2ud9BLxlJLo0+K/tKRHNp8fTCfhSbdiBm5s9nrJ+EjtQneg5mnkOhNJW51\n7fKWcP/AgaG9/K4wZwWAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T02:53:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starre