n":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/baa31b7ac11d053831551b2cd9524447a23f1a8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:25:44Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:25:44Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(worker): give validateRepo its own module\n\nThe audit caught my own relocation on the next run. Parking validateRepo in\nboard-automation.ts (e4ac1a8) pushed that file from under the size threshold to\n520 code lines and firing — which is exactly the \"moving it elsewhere relocates\nthe problem\" the finding warns about, done by me.\n\nIt belongs on its own anyway: it shares nothing with board-automation''s D1 work,\nand the two groups that need it want a GitHub probe, not the activation\ninternals. board-automation.ts is back to its previous size and off the briefing.\n\nVerified: repo-validate-verify 27/27, all 19 worker harnesses green, and the\ngenerated openapi.json still byte-identical to origin/main''s.","tree":{"sha":"aaf9047ae182ed73620cc5db9d77ebbf80be8a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/aaf9047ae182ed73620cc5db9d77ebbf80be8a82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/baa31b7ac11d053831551b2cd9524447a23f1a8e","verification":{"payload":"tree aaf9047ae182ed73620cc5db9d77ebbf80be8a82\nparent e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787095544 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787095544 -0700\n\nrefactor(worker): give validateRepo its own module\n\nThe audit caught my own relocation on the next run. Parking validateRepo in\nboard-automation.ts (e4ac1a8) pushed that file from under the size threshold to\n520 code lines and firing — which is exactly the \"moving it elsewhere relocates\nthe problem\" the finding warns about, done by me.\n\nIt belongs on its own anyway: it shares nothing with board-automation''s D1 work,\nand the two groups that need it want a GitHub probe, not the activation\ninternals. board-automation.ts is back to its previous size and off the briefing.\n\nVerified: repo-validate-verify 27/27, all 19 worker harnesses green, and the\ngenerated openapi.json still byte-identical to origin/main''s.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQG9f3tMFSUveOC22pzNYUcSkXDvOfOcb2bLbsd8SaQuW80wpOdqyGC8MoWs36hWkwf\n2DEFYXr6nsJ1hSY2jYFAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T23:26:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/baa31b7ac11d053831551b2cd9524447a23f1a8e","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGJhYTMxYjdhYzExZDA1MzgzMTU1MWIyY2Q5NTI0NDQ3YTIzZjFhOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82","sha":"e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82"}],"sha":"baa31b7ac11d053831551b2cd9524447a23f1a8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/baa31b7ac11d053831551b2cd9524447a23f1a8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:22:21Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:22:21Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(worker): split the automation routes by concern\n\nvibeCompact size finding: worker/src/routes/automation.ts at 554 code lines,\n532 of them inside `createAutomationRoutes` — 80% of the file in one function,\nwhich the finding rightly says you cannot fix by relocating the function. Cut\ninside it instead, along the seven routes it registers.\n\n  automation.ts            554 -> 34   composes, in the original order\n  automation-reconcile.ts         257   the reconcile-shares sweep\n  automation-activation.ts        157   activate + deactivate\n  automation-repo.ts              129   set-repo + validate\n  automation-reads.ts             113   presets + actionable\n  automation-shared.ts             21   the response wrappers + ref param\n\n`validateRepo` moved to board-automation.ts rather than into a route module:\ntwo groups need it (repo linking probes GitHub, and so does reconcile before it\nmints a share), and board-automation.ts is already where githubToken and the\nactivation internals live.\n\nONE REGISTRAR PER ROUTE, ON PURPOSE\n-----------------------------------\nThe obvious shape — one register function per module — reordered `paths` in the\ngenerated OpenAPI document, because hono emits them in registration order and\nthe domain groups interleave with the original declaration order. Same path set,\nevery path''s content identical, but a different key order in the document\nTenHands codegens from.\n\nSo each module exports a registrar per route and the composer sequences them\nexactly as the file declared them. Verified: the generated openapi.json is now\nBYTE-IDENTICAL to origin/main''s, compared by booting the real worker on both\nsides and stringifying the whole document.\n\nPure code movement otherwise: all 7 route blocks and validateRepo appear\nverbatim in their new homes. Each module imports only the names it uses, so the\n30-line shared import block is gone.\n\nVerified: all 19 worker harnesses green including openapi-verify (100) and the\nrepo-validate coverage added in 36a0499 (27), plus Playwright 147 passed /\n1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"34ab6d8da2154f4a87955f9c803efee8b2232eb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/34ab6d8da2154f4a87955f9c803efee8b2232eb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82","verification":{"payload":"tree 34ab6d8da2154f4a87955f9c803efee8b2232eb3\nparent 36a04999dc5bf6d0890fcf9e064addb9c0c2bbc3\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787095341 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787095341 -0700\n\nrefactor(worker): split the automation routes by concern\n\nvibeCompact size finding: worker/src/routes/automation.ts at 554 code lines,\n532 of them inside `createAutomationRoutes` — 80% of the file in one function,\nwhich the finding rightly says you cannot fix by relocating the function. Cut\ninside it instead, along the seven routes it registers.\n\n  automation.ts            554 -> 34   composes, in the original order\n  automation-reconcile.ts         257   the reconcile-shares sweep\n  automation-activation.ts        157   activate + deactivate\n  automation-repo.ts              129   set-repo + validate\n  automation-reads.ts             113   presets + actionable\n  automation-shared.ts             21   the response wrappers + ref param\n\n`validateRepo` moved to board-automation.ts rather than into a route module:\ntwo groups need it (repo linking probes GitHub, and so does reconcile before it\nmints a share), and board-automation.ts is already where githubToken and the\nactivation internals live.\n\nONE REGISTRAR PER ROUTE, ON PURPOSE\n-----------------------------------\nThe obvious shape — one register function per module — reordered `paths` in the\ngenerated OpenAPI document, because hono emits them in registration order and\nthe domain groups interleave with the original declaration order. Same path set,\nevery path''s content identical, but a different key order in the document\nTenHands codegens from.\n\nSo each module exports a registrar per route and the composer sequences them\nexactly as the file declared them. Verified: the generated openapi.json is now\nBYTE-IDENTICAL to origin/main''s, compared by booting the real worker on both\nsides and stringifying the whole document.\n\nPure code movement otherwise: all 7 route blocks and validateRepo appear\nverbatim in their new homes. Each module imports only the names it uses, so the\n30-line shared import block is gone.\n\nVerified: all 19 worker harnesses green including openapi-verify (100) and the\nrepo-validate coverage added in 36a0499 (27), plus Playwright 147 passed /\n1 skipped.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCuw27uFT1YoboVJZbGtqqbih4XFtKrJekQYUPRhghYfE85bPLQtWnF7KhL9+nyNY7\nSNuSfrJPi1ROzN/G1skAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T23:24:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGU0YWMxYThmNTQ4NjE4NDhmYmQzYTVlMTIyMDdjNzUyNjRhMDBlODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/36a04999dc5bf6d0890fcf9e064addb9c0c2bbc3","sha":"36a04999dc5bf6d0890fcf9e064addb9c0c2bbc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/36a04999dc5bf6d0890fcf9e064addb9c0c2bbc3"}],"sha":"e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/e4ac1a8f54861848fbd3a5e12207c75264a00e82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/36a04999dc5bf6d0890fcf9e064addb9c0c2bbc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:16:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:16:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"test(worker): cover repo validation, which nothing tested\n\nvibeCompact flags worker/src/routes/automation.ts on size, and splitting it\nneeds a test first — so I went looking for what covered each of its seven\nroutes. Six are covered hard: automation-verify, presets-verify and\nactionable-verify drive activate/deactivate, the repo link, presets and the\nactionable scan over real HTTP against a real D1.\n\n`GET /task/api/repos/validate` was covered by nothing. No harness referenced it\nand no Playwright spec did either, despite AutomationPanel calling it every time\nsomeone types a repo into the automation flow. It is also the branchiest code in\nthe file — five outcomes, each with its own user-facing message, one of which\nchanges depending on whether a GitHub token is bound.\n\nCharacterized before it moves: the format check that short-circuits before\nGitHub is ever called, the happy path echoing GitHub''s full_name rather than\nwhat was typed, 404 with and without a token (different messages), 401/403 as\n`token` rather than `error`, any other status as `error`, and a signed-out\ncaller getting a 200 with reason `token` and no GitHub call at all.\n\nGitHub is stubbed via global fetch, which `app.request()` does not route\nthrough, so nothing else in the worker is affected.\n\nConfirmed the assertions have teeth by flipping the 401/403 arm to `error`,\nwhich fails exactly the two checks that name it. 27 assertions, all passing\nagainst today''s code. No production code changed.","tree":{"sha":"22dad911c88bff3dc3b621f3c7b3291b3f49233c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/22dad911c88bff3dc3b621f3c7b3291b3f49233c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/36a04999dc5bf6d0890fcf9e064addb9c0c2bbc3","verification":{"payload":"tree 22dad911c88bff3dc3b621f3c7b3291b3f49233c\nparent f79674c8081487d2dee4588270b42da3450c9916\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787094965 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787094965 -0700\n\ntest(worker): cover repo validation, which nothing tested\n\nvibeCompact flags worker/src/routes/automation.ts on size, and splitting it\nneeds a test first — so I went looking for what covered each of its seven\nroutes. Six are covered hard: automation-verify, presets-verify and\nactionable-verify drive activate/deactivate, the repo link, presets and the\nactionable scan over real HTTP against a real D1.\n\n`GET /task/api/repos/validate` was covered by nothing. No harness referenced it\nand no Playwright spec did either, despite AutomationPanel calling it every time\nsomeone types a repo into the automation flow. It is also the branchiest code in\nthe file — five outcomes, each with its own user-facing message, one of which\nchanges depending on whether a GitHub token is bound.\n\nCharacterized before it moves: the format check that short-circuits before\nGitHub is ever called, the happy path echoing GitHub''s full_name rather than\nwhat was typed, 404 with and without a token (different messages), 401/403 as\n`token` rather than `error`, any other status as `error`, and a signed-out\ncaller getting a 200 with reason `token` and no GitHub call at all.\n\nGitHub is stubbed via global fetch, which `app.request()` does not route\nthrough, so nothing else in the worker is affected.\n\nConfirmed the assertions have teeth by flipping the 401/403 arm to `error`,\nwhich fails exactly the two checks that name it. 27 assertions, all passing\nagainst today''s code. No production code changed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJrFkKHol4zJLWiFmq0rgTQWVH5wTCc23002cPKI/DPCvVtuVR8bLci+6nC1PFLFVy\nwkAwV74tvk/RwE6xSO9wI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T23:24:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/fo