html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/0da1ff1c804ba49baedb3726764b1715f225f891/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:07:15Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:07:15Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(e2e): wait for the board pills to settle, not for the first one\n\nboard-row-mobile failed about one run in three. The beforeEach waited on\n`.pill-btn.first()`, which is satisfied by a single pill, and the tests then\nassert `count > 1` and that none of eight pills escapes the viewport. The wait\nwas weaker than the assertion, so both tests raced the board list''s incremental\npaint.\n\nPolling until more than one pill exists closes the gap. Confirmed pre-existing\nrather than fallout from the handlers split: it reproduces on a pristine\norigin/main checkout too, which is where I went to check before assuming.\n\nTen consecutive runs of the spec, then three full-suite runs, all clean.","tree":{"sha":"203d32032a2d3f9904c2d1f794ebed6eae5e404b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/203d32032a2d3f9904c2d1f794ebed6eae5e404b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/0da1ff1c804ba49baedb3726764b1715f225f891","verification":{"payload":"tree 203d32032a2d3f9904c2d1f794ebed6eae5e404b\nparent 4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787094435 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787094435 -0700\n\nfix(e2e): wait for the board pills to settle, not for the first one\n\nboard-row-mobile failed about one run in three. The beforeEach waited on\n`.pill-btn.first()`, which is satisfied by a single pill, and the tests then\nassert `count > 1` and that none of eight pills escapes the viewport. The wait\nwas weaker than the assertion, so both tests raced the board list''s incremental\npaint.\n\nPolling until more than one pill exists closes the gap. Confirmed pre-existing\nrather than fallout from the handlers split: it reproduces on a pristine\norigin/main checkout too, which is where I went to check before assuming.\n\nTen consecutive runs of the spec, then three full-suite runs, all clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMT4wA35Mf03OSbDmdqxguYJG7oUWtUN6hF42SwTQyNBGya8D78gGqVOGYZ+rG4Y4m\nMtz7iiEP5MWPVXbVRspQk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T23:08:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/0da1ff1c804ba49baedb3726764b1715f225f891","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDBkYTFmZjFjODA0YmE0OWJhZWRiMzcyNjc2NGIxNzE1ZjIyNWY4OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d","sha":"4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d"}],"sha":"0da1ff1c804ba49baedb3726764b1715f225f891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/0da1ff1c804ba49baedb3726764b1715f225f891"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:53:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:53:04Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(domain): split handlers.ts into per-domain modules\n\nvibeCompact size finding: 558 code lines across 18 exported handlers. Unlike\nclient.ts there was no dominant symbol to cut inside — it is a flat collection,\nand the file already carried its own section comments marking exactly where the\ndomains begin. The split follows them, and a sibling for shared helpers\n(handlers-utils.ts) already existed, so the shape was set:\n\n  handlers.ts           782 -> 15   barrel, re-exporting the five modules\n  handlers-batch.ts            232   the three batch writes\n  handlers-tasks.ts            219   create/update/complete/delete\n  handlers-boards.ts           153   board lifecycle + pinned order\n  handlers-reads.ts            153   boards, tasks, stats, calendar\n  handlers-tags.ts              70   the board tag list\n\nhandlers.ts stays a barrel rather than moving callers: `@wolffm/task/api`\nre-exports it as `TaskHandlers`, the worker has 33 call sites across it, and the\nflat surface is what the characterization harness pins. Nothing outside this\ndirectory changes.\n\nPure code movement: reconstructing the five module bodies and diffing against\nthe original file''s corresponding line ranges produces zero differences. Each\nmodule imports only the names it actually uses, so the sprawling shared import\nblock is gone.\n\nVerified against the harness added in 20e8e0e — all 18 exports still present and\ncallable, createTag/deleteTag behaviour unchanged, the batch handlers and task\nlifecycle unchanged: 28 assertions, identical before and after. Plus all 18\nworker harnesses green (these handlers are what they drive over HTTP) and\nPlaywright at 147 passed / 1 skipped.\n\nNew files match the directory''s existing CRLF convention.","tree":{"sha":"6f8740cbd3a521c960d6cdacdd990b64d36d99a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/6f8740cbd3a521c960d6cdacdd990b64d36d99a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f8740cbd3a521c960d6cdacdd990b64d36d99a3\nparent 20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787093584 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787093584 -0700\n\nrefactor(domain): split handlers.ts into per-domain modules\n\nvibeCompact size finding: 558 code lines across 18 exported handlers. Unlike\nclient.ts there was no dominant symbol to cut inside — it is a flat collection,\nand the file already carried its own section comments marking exactly where the\ndomains begin. The split follows them, and a sibling for shared helpers\n(handlers-utils.ts) already existed, so the shape was set:\n\n  handlers.ts           782 -> 15   barrel, re-exporting the five modules\n  handlers-batch.ts            232   the three batch writes\n  handlers-tasks.ts            219   create/update/complete/delete\n  handlers-boards.ts           153   board lifecycle + pinned order\n  handlers-reads.ts            153   boards, tasks, stats, calendar\n  handlers-tags.ts              70   the board tag list\n\nhandlers.ts stays a barrel rather than moving callers: `@wolffm/task/api`\nre-exports it as `TaskHandlers`, the worker has 33 call sites across it, and the\nflat surface is what the characterization harness pins. Nothing outside this\ndirectory changes.\n\nPure code movement: reconstructing the five module bodies and diffing against\nthe original file''s corresponding line ranges produces zero differences. Each\nmodule imports only the names it actually uses, so the sprawling shared import\nblock is gone.\n\nVerified against the harness added in 20e8e0e — all 18 exports still present and\ncallable, createTag/deleteTag behaviour unchanged, the batch handlers and task\nlifecycle unchanged: 28 assertions, identical before and after. Plus all 18\nworker harnesses green (these handlers are what they drive over HTTP) and\nPlaywright at 147 passed / 1 skipped.\n\nNew files match the directory''s existing CRLF convention.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKU9RnEGxftCkr9hmpMx2Iq5lxdJ8miydBe2eNOTYpPBUq6Ax2Cu+f5GWJ7emx+9HT\nMFcLyxzs8G8VxRHaIwEgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T23:08:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDRlNzIwODRjOWVjY2Y0NWUyMGQ3ZTJkNTQzYzU5MTcyODBkZTQzM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841","sha":"20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841"}],"sha":"4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4e72084c9eccf45e20d7e2d543c5917280de433d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:49:34Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:49:34Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"test(domain): characterize handlers.ts, and cover the tag pair nothing tested\n\nvibeCompact flags src/domain/handlers/handlers.ts at 558 code lines across 18\nexported handlers. Splitting it needs a test first, so I went looking for what\nalready covered it — and most of it is covered hard: the worker harnesses drive\nthese handlers over real HTTP against a real SQLite D1, which beats anything a\nunit test would add.\n\nTwo were covered by nothing at all. No harness touches /task/api/tags or\n/task/api/tags/delete, and no Playwright spec deletes a tag, so `createTag` and\n`deleteTag` were reachable only through the UI and asserted nowhere. They now\nhave real behavioural coverage, including the two edges their implementations\nactually encode: createTag is skipIfExists, so re-adding succeeds, says \"already\nexists\" and must not duplicate; deleteTag on an absent tag is a successful no-op.\n\nThe rest pins what a code move can break and the HTTP harnesses might not catch:\nthat all 18 handlers stay exported under the same names, plus behaviour for the\nthree batch handlers — the largest symbols, and the ones about to move — and the\ntask lifecycle they sit on.\n\nThese are pure functions over a Storage interface, so the harness drives them\ndirectly through a small in-memory Storage rather than booting a worker. Writing\nit corrected three assumptions worth recording: createBoard takes `{id, name}`\nnot `{boardId, name}`, TasksFile.tasks is an array rather than a record, and\ngetBoardTasks returns Task[] directly — already filtered to visible — not a\nTasksFile.\n\n28 assertions, all passing against today''s handlers. No production code changed.","tree":{"sha":"846d101daad193d3765183c96646dee9582b332c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/846d101daad193d3765183c96646dee9582b332c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841","verification":{"payload":"tree 846d101daad193d3765183c96646dee9582b332c\nparent 7198e4ae109580f6b857eb55af791df77d98f462\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787093374 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787093374 -0700\n\ntest(domain): characterize handlers.ts, and cover the tag pair nothing tested\n\nvibeCompact flags src/domain/handlers/handlers.ts at 558 code lines across 18\nexported handlers. Splitting it needs a test first, so I went looking for what\nalready covered it — and most of it is covered hard: the worker harnesses drive\nthese handlers over real HTTP against a real SQLite D1, which beats anything a\nunit test would add.\n\nTwo were covered by nothing at all. No harness touches /task/api/tags or\n/task/api/tags/delete, and no Playwright spec deletes a tag, so `createTag` and\n`deleteTag` were reachable only through the UI and asserted nowhere. They now\nhave real behavioural coverage, including the two edges their implementations\nactually encode: createTag is skipIfExists, so re-adding succeeds, says \"already\nexists\" and must not duplicate; deleteTag on an absent tag is a successful no-op.\n\nThe rest pins what a code move can break and the HTTP harnesses might not catch:\nthat all 18 handlers stay exported under the same names, plus behaviour for the\nthree batch handlers — the largest symbols, and the ones about to move — and the\ntask lifecycle they sit on.\n\nThese are pure functions over a Storage interface, so the harness drives them\ndirectly through a small in-memory Storage rather than booting a worker. Writing\nit corrected three assumptions worth recording: createBoard takes `{id, name}`\nnot `{boardId, name}`, TasksFile.tasks is an array rather than a record, and\ngetBoardTasks returns Task[] directly — already filtered to visible — not a\nTasksFile.\n\n28 assertions, all passing against today''s handlers. No production code changed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFKPYRHZFZLNwZz7Sw5OBq5CISVF5h1irohKbB61Qapn7SOPsc9ljEXrFsLsDJK8bT\nrcdDYDJm5jP0yAp/qqKQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T23:08:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDIwZThlMGVhMjU1MzUzZGNiZjVjNTExZWI5YWJmYTQzM2FiYjI4NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/7198e4ae109580f6b857eb55af791df77d98f462","sha":"7198e4ae109580f6b857eb55af791df77d98f462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/7198e4ae109580f6b857eb55af791df77d98f462"}],"sha":"20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/20e8e0ea255353dcbf5c511eb9abfa433abb2841"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/7198e4ae109580f6b857eb55af791df77d98f462/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:34:18Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:34:18Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(vibecompact): record the client.ts fix stamp\n\nMachine-written by `vibecheck audit` at anchor 6cab6c0: size on\nsrc/api/client.ts folds from firing to fixed, and neither the six modules it\nwas split into nor the characterization harness fires anything new.\n\nFive findings remain, all size, all deliberately open.","tree":{"sha":"be2180d4a69f82e30e87d3d90d8db48c2b888747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/be2180d4a69f82e30e87d3d90d8db48c2b888747"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/7198e4ae109580f6b857eb55af791df77d98f462","verification":{"payload":"tree be2180d4a69f82e30e87d3d90d8db48c2b888747\nparent 6cab6c0b64837fa8c29a6743e59b6243961512ca\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092458 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092458 -0700\n\nchore(vibecompact): record the client.ts fix stamp\n\nMachine-written by `vibecheck audit` at anchor 6cab6c0: size on\nsrc/api/client.ts folds from firing to fixed, and neither the six modules it\nwas split into nor the characterization harness fires anything new.\n\nFive findings remain, all size, all deliberately open.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMI3t5lE1PLHkZLtCnHMeLHiKOpLBkgSJro0hp559yEtQlKOcm1udVZnAWWipfSn7D\n6rXFkwFUG7ASli+wCCyQM=\n-----END SSH S