","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6cab6c0b64837fa8c29a6743e59b6243961512ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:33:14Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:33:14Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(api): stop re-exporting ApiCtx from client.ts\n\nThe audit flagged it the run after the split: an unconsumed export, used\ninternally, so un-export rather than delete. It is right — every method group\nimports ApiCtx straight from client-context, and re-exporting it from client.ts\nonly created a second public name for what is an internal seam between the\ngroups. The four types callers do import from here (SyncErrorDetail,\nSyncErrorReporter, CreateApiOptions, TaskUserTier) stay.\n\nVerified: characterization harness 29/29, typecheck and lint clean.","tree":{"sha":"b601eeb01368dc90e8324d1bbd1e1c5f0418153d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/b601eeb01368dc90e8324d1bbd1e1c5f0418153d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/6cab6c0b64837fa8c29a6743e59b6243961512ca","verification":{"payload":"tree b601eeb01368dc90e8324d1bbd1e1c5f0418153d\nparent d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092394 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092394 -0700\n\nrefactor(api): stop re-exporting ApiCtx from client.ts\n\nThe audit flagged it the run after the split: an unconsumed export, used\ninternally, so un-export rather than delete. It is right — every method group\nimports ApiCtx straight from client-context, and re-exporting it from client.ts\nonly created a second public name for what is an internal seam between the\ngroups. The four types callers do import from here (SyncErrorDetail,\nSyncErrorReporter, CreateApiOptions, TaskUserTier) stay.\n\nVerified: characterization harness 29/29, typecheck and lint clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHnn3VA60DQ0nO953TXWy/+fN/i6zVk0CEHSqJY0Lo3Wif+F50KUwFoIAvLKW8I+fD\nuZ+Zznosr73zd3pueJUgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T22:33:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/6cab6c0b64837fa8c29a6743e59b6243961512ca","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDZjYWI2YzBiNjQ4MzdmYThjMjlhNjc0M2U1OWI2MjQzOTYxNTEyY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1","sha":"d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1"}],"sha":"6cab6c0b64837fa8c29a6743e59b6243961512ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/6cab6c0b64837fa8c29a6743e59b6243961512ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:30:44Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:32:03Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(api): split createApi into per-domain method groups\n\nvibeCompact size finding: src/api/client.ts at 791 code lines, 782 of them\ninside `createApi` — 74% of the file in one function, which the finding rightly\nsays you cannot fix by moving the function elsewhere. Cut inside it instead.\n\n`createApi` is a closure: its 27 methods reach for `localStorage`, `userType`,\n`sessionId`, `onSyncError` and the `snapshot` taken before an optimistic write.\nSplitting the methods means naming that closure, which is what ApiCtx in\nclient-context.ts is. The groups are the domains already implicit in the file''s\nown section comments:\n\n  client.ts            81   picks the branch, builds the ctx, composes\n  client-context.ts   286   ApiCtx, the shared helpers, the exported types\n  client-tasks.ts     308   boards sync, tasks, tags — the optimistic writers\n  client-automation   167   presets, activate/deactivate, repo, actionable\n  client-batch.ts     131   the batch writes\n  client-sharing.ts    96   §7 sharing, server-only\n  client-boards.ts     78   board lifecycle + pinned order\n  client-misc.ts       32   validateKey\n\nPure code movement: reconstructing the original `return {...}` block from the\nsix group modules diffs to nothing but the six blank lines at the seams. The\nreturned object is still one flat surface — the groups are spread, not nested —\nso no caller changes, and the public types (SyncErrorDetail, SyncErrorReporter,\nCreateApiOptions, TaskUserTier) are re-exported from client.ts where App.tsx and\nuseTasks already import them.\n\nVerified against the characterization harness added in 99d2727, which pins all\n27 method names and the verb/URL/body each one puts on the wire: 29 assertions,\nidentical before and after. Plus all 17 worker harnesses green and Playwright at\n147 passed / 1 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"6f728024b276a426339b9307cac15f94d2774eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/6f728024b276a426339b9307cac15f94d2774eb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f728024b276a426339b9307cac15f94d2774eb0\nparent a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092244 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092323 -0700\n\nrefactor(api): split createApi into per-domain method groups\n\nvibeCompact size finding: src/api/client.ts at 791 code lines, 782 of them\ninside `createApi` — 74% of the file in one function, which the finding rightly\nsays you cannot fix by moving the function elsewhere. Cut inside it instead.\n\n`createApi` is a closure: its 27 methods reach for `localStorage`, `userType`,\n`sessionId`, `onSyncError` and the `snapshot` taken before an optimistic write.\nSplitting the methods means naming that closure, which is what ApiCtx in\nclient-context.ts is. The groups are the domains already implicit in the file''s\nown section comments:\n\n  client.ts            81   picks the branch, builds the ctx, composes\n  client-context.ts   286   ApiCtx, the shared helpers, the exported types\n  client-tasks.ts     308   boards sync, tasks, tags — the optimistic writers\n  client-automation   167   presets, activate/deactivate, repo, actionable\n  client-batch.ts     131   the batch writes\n  client-sharing.ts    96   §7 sharing, server-only\n  client-boards.ts     78   board lifecycle + pinned order\n  client-misc.ts       32   validateKey\n\nPure code movement: reconstructing the original `return {...}` block from the\nsix group modules diffs to nothing but the six blank lines at the seams. The\nreturned object is still one flat surface — the groups are spread, not nested —\nso no caller changes, and the public types (SyncErrorDetail, SyncErrorReporter,\nCreateApiOptions, TaskUserTier) are re-exported from client.ts where App.tsx and\nuseTasks already import them.\n\nVerified against the characterization harness added in 99d2727, which pins all\n27 method names and the verb/URL/body each one puts on the wire: 29 assertions,\nidentical before and after. Plus all 17 worker harnesses green and Playwright at\n147 passed / 1 skipped.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCISb4f3jTJhsQfIAZw5QCt99yCEuAZmYLLSBV02QWba1hgoORHGd2mosN6mZIcfz3\nIoyYRiZ/lgPPo8hZsDPgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T22:32:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGQxMjBhY2UwN2ExM2E2MmYwZTVkZDY4MjM5N2NhMGQ4ZjY4NmI1ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440","sha":"a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440"}],"sha":"d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/d120ace07a13a62f0e5dd682397ca0d8f686b5d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:26:20Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:32:03Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"test(api): characterize src/api/client.ts before splitting it\n\nvibeCompact flags client.ts at 791 code lines, 782 of them inside `createApi`.\nSplitting it needs a test first, and the only thing exercising those 27 methods\ntoday is Playwright driving the whole app — which covers the paths a user walks\nand nothing else. The risk in moving a method between modules is not a loud\nbreak; it is one of the 27 quietly changing the request it sends, or ceasing to\nbe returned, on a path no spec happens to click.\n\nSo this pins the observable contract and nothing about the implementation: the\nexact method surface, the public-vs-syncing branch, and for each method the\nverb, URL and body it puts on the wire, against a recording fetch stub and an\nin-memory localStorage.\n\nLands in src/test/, which run-worker-verify.mjs already scans alongside\nworker/test — so `pnpm run test:worker` picks it up and CI runs it. Unlike\nworker/test, src/** IS covered by the app''s tsconfig, so it typechecks too.\n\nWriting it corrected four things I had assumed wrong, which is the point of\ncharacterizing before refactoring rather than after:\n\n- createTask POSTs /task/api with boardId in the BODY, not a query param.\n- batchUpdateTags PATCHes the LEGACY alias /task/api/batch-tag, not\n  /boards/{id}/tasks/batch/update-tags. batchMoveTasks likewise posts\n  /task/api/batch-move, not /batch/move-tasks. Both aliases are live on the\n  worker; which one the client sends is the contract, so both are pinned.\n- The optimistic writes fire their fetch WITHOUT awaiting it, so recorded calls\n  only settle after the microtask queue drains.\n- patch/complete/delete read the cached task first — so a refusal can put it\n  back — and throw TaskNotFoundError against a cache that does not hold it. The\n  seed task must also be created AFTER the syncFromApi checks, because a sync\n  replaces the cached board with the stub''s copy, which carries no tasks.\n\n29 assertions, all passing against today''s client. No production code changed.","tree":{"sha":"0eade14452896b01f1631ade00feccdd5543f9b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/0eade14452896b01f1631ade00feccdd5543f9b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440","verification":{"payload":"tree 0eade14452896b01f1631ade00feccdd5543f9b8\nparent 59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787091980 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787092323 -0700\n\ntest(api): characterize src/api/client.ts before splitting it\n\nvibeCompact flags client.ts at 791 code lines, 782 of them inside `createApi`.\nSplitting it needs a test first, and the only thing exercising those 27 methods\ntoday is Playwright driving the whole app — which covers the paths a user walks\nand nothing else. The risk in moving a method between modules is not a loud\nbreak; it is one of the 27 quietly changing the request it sends, or ceasing to\nbe returned, on a path no spec happens to click.\n\nSo this pins the observable contract and nothing about the implementation: the\nexact method surface, the public-vs-syncing branch, and for each method the\nverb, URL and body it puts on the wire, against a recording fetch stub and an\nin-memory localStorage.\n\nLands in src/test/, which run-worker-verify.mjs already scans alongside\nworker/test — so `pnpm run test:worker` picks it up and CI runs it. Unlike\nworker/test, src/** IS covered by the app''s tsconfig, so it typechecks too.\n\nWriting it corrected four things I had assumed wrong, which is the point of\ncharacterizing before refactoring rather than after:\n\n- createTask POSTs /task/api with boardId in the BODY, not a query param.\n- batchUpdateTags PATCHes the LEGACY alias /task/api/batch-tag, not\n  /boards/{id}/tasks/batch/update-tags. batchMoveTasks likewise posts\n  /task/api/batch-move, not /batch/move-tasks. Both aliases are live on the\n  worker; which one the client sends is the contract, so both are pinned.\n- The optimistic writes fire their fetch WITHOUT awaiting it, so recorded calls\n  only settle after the microtask queue drains.\n- patch/complete/delete read the cached task first — so a refusal can put it\n  back — and throw TaskNotFoundError against a cache that does not hold it. The\n  seed task must also be created AFTER the syncFromApi checks, because a sync\n  replaces the cached board with the stub''s copy, which carries no tasks.\n\n29 assertions, all passing against today''s client. No production code changed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKTeF7CN68R/X4Q0mMC8tjxLPlS4Ty4riMJzEqRIRrKGwxMFSXtxSIGUltAdpQGMUG\nnSSZP8WFsRf53iKEalqwI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T22:32:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKGExOGNiZTBiNGE0YjM1YzUxMTg5M2ZlZDY1MzBhMTZlOTM3NDk0NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3","sha":"59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3"}],"sha":"a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/a18cbe0b4a4b35c511893fed6530a16e93749440"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:38:32Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:38:32Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore(release): @wolffm/themes@5.7.8 @wolffm/task@5.9.15 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"68c6cc77118b18d462c8314fded618fce3de6493","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/68c6cc77118b18d462c8314fded618fce3de6493"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3","node_id":"C_kwDOP50_wNoAKDU5ZjNhYmJhY2JmODgwOTg0ZDZkNTc1NmZhMzJiMDc5ZmFhYWUxZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-task/commit/4708723a583d1671c4e672c865222dd1a2ade64f","sha":"4708723a583d1671c4e672c865222dd1a2ade64f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4708723a583d1671c4e672c865222dd1a2ade64f"}],"sha":"59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/59f3abbacbf880984d6d5756fa32b079faaae1d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/commits/4708723a583d1671c4e672c865222dd1a2ade64f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:37:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:37:34Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(themes): see an emoji that CLOSES a text run, in both tools\n\nEvery markup rule in check-icons and the codemod anchored on what comes BEFORE a\nglyph — `>`, line start, `{'' ''}`. A glyph sitting AFTER its label was invisible to\nboth. pygmalion reported clean across 268 files while shipping a raw `▶` in\nBakeoffReview, and the codemod said nothing about the same line.\n\nI previously said check-icons caught these and only the codemod was blind. That\nwas wrong: the gate has the identical hole, which is worse, because a green gate\nis the thing everyone trusts.\n\nBoth now match a token anchored on the whitespace before it and a `<` or\nend-of-line after it. The token class excludes quotes and braces, so `''⚠ '' + err`\nand `className=\"a b\"` cannot produce one.\n\nThe rule needed a second guard the leading rules never did. `isNonUi`/`isNonUiLine`\nonly catch lines that BEGIN with a comment marker, so a TRAILING comment still\nreads as code — and pygmalion''s icons.tsx annotates its whole registry that way:\n`export const WarnIcon = TriangleAlert // ⚠`. Without it the codemod rewrote that\ncomment into `// <Icon name=\"warning\" />`, turning prose about an icon into an\nicon. Both tools now stop at a quote-aware `//` boundary, so a `//` inside a\nstring is not mistaken for one. The pair guard honours it too, or emoji in\ncomments would defer real conversions on nearby lines.\n\nMeasured across fifteen repos before shipping. The gate gains exactly one finding\n— pygmalion''s BakeoffReview:310, a real raw `▶` — and nothing else anywhere. The\ncodemod''s replacement counts are unchanged everywhere, hadoku-trader''s single\nconversion included. Fixtures cover trailing conversion, trailing refusal,\ntrailing comments, strings, attributes, and the `https://` case where a `//`\ninside a string precedes a real comment.","tree":{"sha":"1bee628736982cd4d4e72501bbe74389f74e26cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/trees/1bee628736982cd4d4e72501bbe74389f74e26cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-task/git/commits/4708723a583d1671c4e672c865222dd1a2ade64f","verification":{"payload":"tree 1bee628736982cd4d4e72501bbe74389f74e26cb\nparent 48268dd863a2134ecf0ae1bf1b522bec1744a4ea\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787089046 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787089054 -0700\n\nfix(themes): see an emoji that CLOSES a text run, in both tools\n\nEvery markup rule in check-icons and the codemod anchored on what comes BEFORE a\nglyph — `>`, line start, `{'' ''}`. A glyph sitting AFTER its label was invisible to\nboth. pygmalion reported clean across 268 files while shipping a raw `▶` in\nBakeoffReview, and the codemod said nothing about the same line.\n\nI previously said check-icons caught these and only the codemod was blind. That\nwas wrong: the gate has the identical hole, which is worse, because a green gate\nis the thing everyone trusts.\n\nBoth now match a token anchored on the whitespace before it and a `<` or\nend-of-line after it. The token class excludes quotes and braces, so `''⚠ '' + err`\nand `className=\"a b\"` cannot produce one.\n\nThe rule needed a second guard the leading rules never did. `isNonUi`/`isNonUiLine`\nonly catch lines that BEGIN with a comment marker, so a TRAILING comment still\nreads as code — and pygmalion''s icons.tsx annotates its whole registry that way:\n`export const WarnIcon = TriangleAlert // ⚠`. Without it the codemod rewrote that\ncomment into `// <Icon name=\"warning\" />`, turning prose about an icon into an\nicon. Both tools now stop at a quote-aware `//` boundary, so a `//` inside a\nstring is not mistaken for one. The pair guard honours it too, or emoji in\ncomments would defer real conversions on nearby lines.\n\nMeasured across fifteen repos before shipping. The gate gains exactly one finding\n— pygmalion''s BakeoffReview:310, a real raw `▶` — and nothing else anywhere. The\ncodemod''s replacement counts are unchanged everywhere, hadoku-trader''s single\nconversion included. Fixtures cover trailing conversion, trailing refusal,\ntrailing comments, strings, attributes, and the `https://` case where a `//`\ninside a string precedes a real comment.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEg+drmmLTw/p+QRVZydPxbre599gwwt/0nwxmxihix2gBKkN+1Eer6uRCuPl0jiHG\n2eGC+dDDl+1XWkcoss6Qc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T21:37:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/receiv