g_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/3805547d1221a730115964572ccf4b816627f6da","node_id":"C_kwDOP53cGNoAKDM4MDU1NDdkMTIyMWE3MzAxMTU5NjQ1NzJjY2Y0YjgxNjYyN2Y2ZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/3bb6705d84c7283b16dd3f67b4572319f5aa389d","sha":"3bb6705d84c7283b16dd3f67b4572319f5aa389d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/3bb6705d84c7283b16dd3f67b4572319f5aa389d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/a403de55d3c749eadbeb7ccfaaf063d3ee74bc15","sha":"a403de55d3c749eadbeb7ccfaaf063d3ee74bc15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/a403de55d3c749eadbeb7ccfaaf063d3ee74bc15"}],"sha":"3805547d1221a730115964572ccf4b816627f6da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/3805547d1221a730115964572ccf4b816627f6da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/1ecf883ff70ab9a127793844e5a17447befc355b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:57:12Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:57:12Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"message":"fix(academics): make emisStudentId settable on update, with its invariants (#480)\n\nCEHRD issues the student IEMIS ID after Flash I, so recording it on an\nexisting student is the normal lifecycle rather than a remediation path.\nThat path did not work: updateStudentDtoToEntity is an explicit allow-list\nand omitted the field, so PATCH /students/:id carrying an emisStudentId\nreturned 200, discarded it, and echoed the previous value back.\n\nThe issue reported the field as written verbatim into an unindexed,\nunvalidated attribute. It never reached that loop. Nothing was written at\nall, which is better for data integrity than reported and worse for\nhonesty: the operator is told a remediation succeeded when nothing\nhappened.\n\nThat changes what this fix is. The asks in #480 are not repairs of\nexisting corruption; they are preconditions for enabling the field.\nAdding it to the mapper alone would create precisely the defect the issue\ndescribes, so the mapper change and the invariants land together:\n\n- Write-once. null -> value is allowed, value -> same value stays\n  idempotent, value -> different and value -> cleared are refused. Same\n  argument that made emisSchoolCode immutable: re-pointing detaches a\n  pupil from their federal record. A mistyped ID is therefore permanent\n  by design; remediating one belongs behind an audited system-admin\n  override, as tenantTag already documents, not a silent overwrite.\n- Tenant uniqueness, via the same findByEmisStudentId GSI7 lookup the\n  create path runs, excluding the student''s own row.\n- GSI7 sparse-index keys written alongside the attribute. They are\n  derived attributes the service must write explicitly; without them a\n  remediated student carries the ID but is invisible to\n  findByEmisStudentId, and so to IEMIS import dedup and to the uniqueness\n  check above.\n\nBecause clearing a set value is refused, the issue''s third bullet —\nREMOVE stale GSI7 keys on clear — is unreachable by construction rather\nthan unimplemented. I would rather not carry a branch nothing can trigger.\n\nUnblocks #481, which needs setting the ID later to be the primary\nlifecycle, and shoaibrain/edforge-saas-frontend#365, whose field should\nrender read-only once set.","tree":{"sha":"737ea647516bf1992da41dbcce3fcb7f6330ec07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/trees/737ea647516bf1992da41dbcce3fcb7f6330ec07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/commits/1ecf883ff70ab9a127793844e5a17447befc355b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/1ecf883ff70ab9a127793844e5a17447befc355b","node_id":"C_kwDOP53cGNoAKDFlY2Y4ODNmZjcwYWI5YTEyNzc5Mzg0NGU1YTE3NDQ3YmVmYzM1NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/3bb6705d84c7283b16dd3f67b4572319f5aa389d","sha":"3bb6705d84c7283b16dd3f67b4572319f5aa389d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/3bb6705d84c7283b16dd3f67b4572319f5aa389d"}],"sha":"1ecf883ff70ab9a127793844e5a17447befc355b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/1ecf883ff70ab9a127793844e5a17447befc355b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/a403de55d3c749eadbeb7ccfaaf063d3ee74bc15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:50:17Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T20:50:17Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"message":"docs(deploys): school reads scope to role assignments — prod green\n\nRecords the #492 deploy (issue #484). GET /schools and the two sibling\nby-id reads were tenant-scoped only, so any authenticated principal —\nincluding a parent — received every school in the tenant with its\ngovernment IEMIS code and contact details.\n\nThe entry keeps the part that matters for the next reviewer: the authz\naudit passed before and after, because the routes were allowlisted under\n\"authenticated tenant-scoped reference reads\". That category, not the\nhandler, is the root cause.\n\nValidation is recorded for both principal types, including the detail\nthat the tenant-wide principal holds no explicit assignments — which is\nwhat makes it evidence that the short-circuit works rather than evidence\nthat assignments happen to cover everything.\n\nPasses npm run lint:deploy-evidence.","tree":{"sha":"4d3a562507b722293f9a9801e7adba64bb9c7f3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/trees/4d3a562507b722293f9a9801e7adba64bb9c7f3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/commits/a403de55d3c749eadbeb7ccfaaf063d3ee74bc15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_use