:[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5","sha":"3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7","sha":"7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7"}],"sha":"70273f9833debb339c39883cb019331f85f2829f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/70273f9833debb339c39883cb019331f85f2829f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/7ee35bd95b1808559ed2132a942802111a03f86a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:36:52Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:36:52Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"message":"feat(finance): server-side invoice-number lookup on GSI3\n\nBackend half of #348.\n\nThe invoices search box filtered only the rows the client had already\nloaded. With 1,423 invoices in the school and 50 on the page, pasting a\nreal, issued, paid invoice number returned \"No results\" — the single most\ncommon finance lookup telling an operator their invoice does not exist.\n\nThere was no server-side lookup to call. The list endpoint accepted no such\nparameter, and GSI3 (`gsi3pk = TENANT#{tid}#SCHOOL#{sid}`,\n`gsi3sk = INVNUM#{number}`) — the index built for exactly this access\npattern and populated unconditionally on every invoice — had zero readers.\n\n`GET .../invoices?invoiceNumber=` now routes to that index:\n\n- a prefix match on the sort key, so a pasted number and the leading part\n  of one both work;\n- no FilterExpression, so it cannot starve a page the way the filtered\n  paths did (#466);\n- whitespace trimmed, since operators paste from receipts and bank\n  references; a blank value falls through to the normal listing.\n\nParent and Student callers keep their scoping. Their branch stays on the\nper-student GSI2 partitions and applies the number as a narrowing filter\nthere, so a number can never widen what a parent can reach. A new assertion\nin the parent-scope spec pins that.\n\nNo spec change: query parameters are not declared on this route (`status`,\n`billingSource` and the rest are equally absent) and API Gateway passes\nquery strings verbatim to a Lambda proxy integration. No schema, GSI, IAM\nor shared-types change — GSI3 already exists and is already populated.\n\nThe parent-scope spec calls the controller positionally, so adding the\nparameter shifted its arguments and broke five assertions. Fixture updated\nand all five re-verified; the scoping logic itself is untouched.\n\nGates: 239 suites / 3,696 tests green; nest build finance + identity +\nacademics; typecheck:cdk clean; lint 0 errors; route-drift 4/4; generated\nOpenAPI current.\n\nThe operator-visible fix lands with the frontend change that calls this.","tree":{"sha":"1357462f8b3efb80166d7f2bc7eba5ee4712a10b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/trees/1357462f8b3efb80166d7f2bc7eba5ee4712a10b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/commits/7ee35bd95b1808559ed2132a942802111a03f86a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/7ee35bd95b1808559ed2132a942802111a03f86a","node_id":"C_kwDOP53cGNoAKDdlZTM1YmQ5NWIxODA4NTU5ZWQyMTMyYTk0MjgwMjExMWEwM2Y4NmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5","sha":"3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5"}],"sha":"7ee35bd95b1808559ed2132a942802111a03f86a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/7ee35bd95b1808559ed2132a942802111a03f86a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:11:26Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:11:26Z","email":"rainshoaib2013@outlook.com","name":"Shoaib Rain"},"message":"feat(finance): bulk preview prices agreements the way generation bills them\n\nBackend half of #465.\n\nThe wizard previewed agreement-covered students at catalog rates, so a\nfamily on a NPR 20,000 agreement previewed at NPR 33,000 — a 65% overstatement\nof what would actually be billed. It also reported 0 duplicates for students\nthe once-per-term guard rejects outright, so the operator was told they were\neligible when generation would 409 every one of them.\n\nRoot cause of the money half: bulk-preview returned no amounts at all. The\ncaller totalled the batch from catalog fee structures, because the preview\ntold it which students were on an agreement but not what the agreement\ncharges them.\n\nThe preview now answers both questions:\n\n- `students[]` rows gain `suppressedFeeStructureIds` (which requested\n  structures the agreement replaces), `agreementAmount` (what replaces them)\n  and `coveredFeeTypes`. A caller totals a batch as\n  catalog(requested NOT suppressed) + agreementAmount.\n- `agreementBlocked` marks a student whose agreement already priced this\n  term. Those students are excluded from `eligibleCount` and counted in a\n  new `agreementBlockedCount`. It is kept separate from `duplicateCount`\n  because the reasons differ, and the two sets are unioned for eligibility\n  so a student who is both is not subtracted twice.\n\nThe money math is now shared rather than reimplemented. `planAgreementPricing`\n(what gets billed) and `bulkPreview` (what the operator is shown) both call\n`agreementReplacementLines`, so the preview cannot drift from the bill — two\nimplementations of the same money question is exactly how this bug happened.\nThe once-per-term check is likewise split into a non-throwing\n`findAgreementInvoiceConflict`, reused by the throwing assert, so the preview\ncan ask without raising.\n\nRows for students with no agreement keep the pre-FB shape exactly. Everything\nadded is optional and best-effort: a resolution failure omits the fields and\nleaves the student eligible rather than failing the preview.\n\nNo schema, route, IAM or shared-types change — the contract is the\ncontroller''s inline response type, so no npm publish is involved.\n\nGates: 239 suites / 3,699 tests green; nest build finance + identity +\nacademics; typecheck:cdk clean; lint 0 errors; route-drift 4/4. The 42\nagreement and golden tests pass unchanged, which is what proves the\nextraction did not move any billed number.\n\nThe operator-visible total closes with the frontend change that consumes\nthese fields; this PR only makes the data available.","tree":{"sha":"c5c6daa41be1b0efd056d599bb8775de05f10f5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/trees/c5c6daa41be1b0efd056d599bb8775de05f10f5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/git/commits/7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain","id":59787578,"login":"shoaibrain","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Nzg3NTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shoaibrain","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7","node_id":"C_kwDOP53cGNoAKDcyODAzMTNjNDQ0NDdkN2NjMmQwZmRiODIwNzU1NTczZWQ4NDQyZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shoaibrain/edforge/commit/3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5","sha":"3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/3e6576d60aabdc9f498791ac77335c4105db59e5"}],"sha":"7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shoaibrain/edforge/commits/7280313c44447d7cc2d0fdb820755573ed8442f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59787578?v=4","events_url":"htt